<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<tt xml:lang="en" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml" xmlns:ttm="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#metadata" xmlns:tts="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#styling" xmlns:ttp="http://www.w3.org/ns/ttml#parameter" ttp:profile="http://www.w3.org/TR/profile/sdp-us" >
<head>
<styling>
<style xml:id="s1" tts:textAlign="center" tts:extent="90% 90%" tts:origin="5% 5%" tts:displayAlign="after"/>
<style xml:id="s2" tts:fontSize=".72c" tts:backgroundColor="black" tts:color="white"/>
</styling>
<layout>
<region xml:id="r1" style="s1"/>
</layout>
</head>
<body region="r1">
<div>
<p begin="00:00:00.640" end="00:00:08.080" style="s2">The Astl realm is steeped in Aia. Mages are <br />everywhere. Elemental mages, blade casters,  </p>
<p begin="00:00:08.080" end="00:00:19.440" style="s2">body addexs, summoners. <br />Everyone chases the next rank</p>
<p begin="00:00:19.440" end="00:00:24.400" style="s2">here. Talent sets your starting <br />line, resolve sets your ceiling,  </p>
<p begin="00:00:24.400" end="00:00:28.320" style="s2">but power is the only past that matters.</p>
<p begin="00:00:36.160" end="00:00:46.640" style="s2">Is Astall&#39;s entrance trial really that <br />hard? Are all of you multi-attried agents?</p>
<p begin="00:00:46.640" end="00:00:54.880" style="s2">None of you were born with a bonded focus. Your <br />bonded blades can&#39;t even split into more blades.  </p>
<p begin="00:00:54.880" end="00:00:58.680" style="s2">Then controlling a few flying blades at <br />once has to be normal, right? [sighs]  </p>
<p begin="00:01:00.560" end="00:01:04.880" style="s2">Are you messing with us? Any one of those gifts <br />would make you a once- in a generation prodigy.  </p>
<p begin="00:01:04.880" end="00:01:13.200" style="s2">The faculty would fight over you. Someone <br />like that wouldn&#39;t be standing in this line.</p>
<p begin="00:01:13.200" end="00:01:24.400" style="s2">So that counts as genius out here. <br />My papers told me the exact opposite.</p>
<p begin="00:01:28.200" end="00:01:29.200" style="s2">[music]</p>
<p begin="00:01:29.200" end="00:01:45.680" style="s2">Ice aspect formed.</p>
<p begin="00:01:45.680" end="00:01:50.720" style="s2">Fire aspect. Gather.</p>
<p begin="00:01:55.080" end="00:01:56.080" style="s2">[sighs]</p>
<p begin="00:01:56.080" end="00:02:11.360" style="s2">Blaze to me.</p>
<p begin="00:02:11.360" end="00:02:15.360" style="s2">Nina,</p>
<p begin="00:02:15.360" end="00:02:20.080" style="s2">papers. Good. You&#39;ve mastered <br />all six arcanic affinities. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="00:02:20.080" end="00:02:25.680" style="s2">you&#39;re finally a proper elemental mage. <br />So, I can leave the village now. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="00:02:25.680" end="00:02:29.360" style="s2">the outside world is full of prodigies and <br />powerful mages. You can only control two blades.  </p>
<p begin="00:02:29.360" end="00:02:36.320" style="s2">You&#39;d get crushed out there. [laughter] [snorts] <br />But you took me in 15 years ago, and I&#39;ve trained  </p>
<p begin="00:02:36.320" end="00:02:42.080" style="s2">in Evergreen Village every day since. I&#39;ve never <br />even been beyond the hills. Please, Papa Alder,  </p>
<p begin="00:02:42.080" end="00:02:50.160" style="s2">let me go. All right. But if you run into trouble <br />you can&#39;t handle, call for us. Yes, Astable Realm,  </p>
<p begin="00:02:50.160" end="00:02:56.720" style="s2">here I come. I, Nina Rowan, am going to be the <br />greatest healer alive. Prodigies everywhere,  </p>
<p begin="00:02:56.720" end="00:03:01.520" style="s2">monsters on every corner. They lied to me. All <br />I&#39;ve wanted since I came to this world was to  </p>
<p begin="00:03:01.520" end="00:03:05.600" style="s2">be a healer. Those old men swore I&#39;d die the <br />second I left, unless I trained from dawn to  </p>
<p begin="00:03:05.600" end="00:03:12.960" style="s2">midnight. 15 years of that, and now I&#39;m a six <br />affinity mage who fights with blades. Silence.</p>
<p begin="00:03:12.960" end="00:03:18.000" style="s2">The entrance selection begins now. <br />Step forward in order and place your  </p>
<p begin="00:03:18.000" end="00:03:25.520" style="s2">palm on the testing pillar. It will <br />reveal your affinition and rank.</p>
<p begin="00:03:25.520" end="00:03:31.000" style="s2">She talks big. Let&#39;s see what rank <br />this idiot actually is. [laughter]  </p>
<p begin="00:03:31.600" end="00:03:48.000" style="s2">All that talk and she&#39;s a used</p>
<p begin="00:03:48.000" end="00:03:50.800" style="s2">Good. I held it back. If <br />all six affinities lit up,  </p>
<p begin="00:03:50.800" end="00:03:58.160" style="s2">that pillar might have exploded. [snorts] <br />Age 15. Third rank light mage. Affinity 96.  </p>
<p begin="00:03:58.960" end="00:04:03.840" style="s2">That&#39;s incredible. You could count a students <br />with affinity that high on one hand. So what?  </p>
<p begin="00:04:03.840" end="00:04:08.080" style="s2">She&#39;s a light affinitive healer. High affinity <br />doesn&#39;t make her useful. Even the best healing  </p>
<p begin="00:04:08.080" end="00:04:14.800" style="s2">spell can&#39;t beat a good elixir. In Astall, power <br />is what matters. The stronger the affinity,  </p>
<p begin="00:04:14.800" end="00:04:18.480" style="s2">the greater the talent. With a score like <br />yours, your healing and purification magic  </p>
<p begin="00:04:18.480" end="00:04:24.560" style="s2">will far surpass other mages of your rank. A pity <br />light magic is built for healing. If only you were  </p>
<p begin="00:04:24.560" end="00:04:29.680" style="s2">a blade caster. A bladecast? I&#39;ve been one for <br />years. But what&#39;s so special about that? My dream  </p>
<p begin="00:04:29.680" end="00:04:41.440" style="s2">is to become the greatest healer in Astl. Take <br />this. The thousandst step trial is just ahead.</p>
<p begin="00:04:41.440" end="00:04:48.400" style="s2">The trial has 999 visible steps. It is the <br />final entrance test, and the resistance rises  </p>
<p begin="00:04:48.400" end="00:04:55.520" style="s2">with your rank. A light magent only needs to <br />reach step 150 to pass. If I move fast, I can  </p>
<p begin="00:04:55.520" end="00:05:08.720" style="s2">still make lunch. I heard Astall&#39;s wind house is <br />unbelievably tender. I&#39;m not missing that. Stop.</p>
<p begin="00:05:08.720" end="00:05:12.960" style="s2">White uniforms with red trend. They&#39;re bonded <br />proteges from the inner houses. I know that girl,  </p>
<p begin="00:05:12.960" end="00:05:16.320" style="s2">Livia Vale, the youngest member of House <br />Storm Glass, their only female protege and  </p>
<p begin="00:05:16.320" end="00:05:21.120" style="s2">a fourth ranked Bladecaster at 15. Housem Storm <br />treats her like a princess. Look at the seniors  </p>
<p begin="00:05:21.120" end="00:05:25.600" style="s2">guarding her. Every one of them could dominate <br />a dueling bracket and they&#39;re all orbiting her.</p>
<p begin="00:05:33.680" end="00:05:41.280" style="s2">You You murdered my mother and crippled my father. <br />Today I kill you for both of them. Me? You don&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="00:05:41.280" end="00:05:44.720" style="s2">waste words on her. She hasn&#39;t enrolled <br />yet. Kill her and settle the debt. Livia,  </p>
<p begin="00:05:44.720" end="00:05:49.760" style="s2">there must be a mistake. Your father, Victor Vale, <br />is a fifth ranked fire mag. Your mother, Serena,  </p>
<p begin="00:05:49.760" end="00:05:53.920" style="s2">was a fourth ranked light magent. This girl is <br />only third rank and light a fraction. How could  </p>
<p begin="00:05:53.920" end="00:05:58.960" style="s2">she have killed your mother and defeated your <br />father? The blood compass doesn&#39;t lie. It was her.  </p>
<p begin="00:05:58.960" end="00:06:02.800" style="s2">Maybe a useless light mage couldn&#39;t do it herself, <br />but she could have hired someone to murder my  </p>
<p begin="00:06:02.800" end="00:06:09.600" style="s2">mother and ruin my father. Your mother is dead. <br />Your father gets to live with what he did. 15  </p>
<p begin="00:06:09.600" end="00:06:15.200" style="s2">years ago, they tried to kill my mother and steal <br />my life. That was me. Yesterday, I collected the  </p>
<p begin="00:06:15.200" end="00:06:21.680" style="s2">debt. Fair, isn&#39;t it? Liar. My mother was kind. <br />She would never kill anyone. And if she did,  </p>
<p begin="00:06:21.680" end="00:06:29.520" style="s2">your mother must have deserved it. Kind. Fine. <br />Let&#39;s show everyone exactly how kind she was.  </p>
<p begin="00:06:29.520" end="00:06:34.560" style="s2">Helena Rowan, for the sake of our years together, <br />give birth to the child. Let her serve as a proxy  </p>
<p begin="00:06:34.560" end="00:06:38.800" style="s2">vessel for Serena&#39;s baby, and I&#39;ll make your death <br />painless. Helena, listen to your husband. Dying  </p>
<p begin="00:06:38.800" end="00:06:46.240" style="s2">in place of my child would be an honor for your <br />little girl, Victor Veil. I would rather die than  </p>
<p begin="00:06:46.240" end="00:07:00.000" style="s2">let you sacrifice my daughter for that bastard <br />child. No, she&#39;s going to detonate her core.</p>
<p begin="00:07:00.000" end="00:07:04.480" style="s2">Your mother stole another woman&#39;s husband and <br />tried to murder a pregnant woman. Your father  </p>
<p begin="00:07:04.480" end="00:07:08.400" style="s2">abandoned his wife and meant to turn his own <br />daughter into a sacrificial vessel. He drove  </p>
<p begin="00:07:08.400" end="00:07:12.480" style="s2">his wife to her death and tried to sacrifice his <br />own daughter. Was a monster. Worse than Rogue  </p>
<p begin="00:07:12.480" end="00:07:18.400" style="s2">Warlax. They deserved it. No, my parents aren&#39;t <br />like that. Insult them again and I&#39;ll kill you.  </p>
<p begin="00:07:18.400" end="00:07:22.800" style="s2">Frost Bloom. A legendary grade bonded blade. <br />Housemaster Stormy actually gave it to her.  </p>
<p begin="00:07:22.800" end="00:07:26.080" style="s2">They say it was forged from thousand-year <br />frost crystal. Afall has nothing else like  </p>
<p begin="00:07:26.080" end="00:07:29.680" style="s2">it. Frostbloom never leaves its sheath without <br />drawing to kill her. A third wrangle light mage  </p>
<p begin="00:07:29.680" end="00:07:32.400" style="s2">against a fourth evil blade cluster with <br />a legendary weapon. That girl won&#39;t even  </p>
<p begin="00:07:32.400" end="00:07:43.920" style="s2">get away. You will not draw a blade here without <br />sanction. [screaming] Glacial arc. You kill me.</p>
<p begin="00:07:47.840" end="00:07:53.120" style="s2">Youth is amazing. She can <br />fall asleep anywhere. Livia,  </p>
<p begin="00:07:53.120" end="00:07:58.720" style="s2">you used a black market relic on a bonded <br />protege of house stormfight. Three blade  </p>
<p begin="00:07:58.720" end="00:08:09.760" style="s2">hasters. Light magic alone could get <br />annoying. Do I actually draw a blade?</p>
<p begin="00:08:09.760" end="00:08:14.880" style="s2">Now this is interesting. Three blade hasters <br />ganging up on one helpless light magic. How  </p>
<p begin="00:08:14.880" end="00:08:20.640" style="s2">impressive. Housemaster Stormy must be <br />so proud of his students. Mentor win. Are  </p>
<p begin="00:08:20.640" end="00:08:24.880" style="s2">you really going to interfere in how Storm <br />business without cause? Interfering without  </p>
<p begin="00:08:24.880" end="00:08:35.840" style="s2">cause would be rude. Girl, want to mentor a <br />terrifying woman in red. I love her. Mentor.</p>
<p begin="00:08:35.840" end="00:08:39.200" style="s2">Good girl. She is now my bonded prodigy.  </p>
<p begin="00:08:39.200" end="00:08:42.880" style="s2">Try bullying her again because she&#39;s alone <br />and you&#39;ll answer to me. She attacked our  </p>
<p begin="00:08:42.880" end="00:08:49.120" style="s2">youngest protege. Are you seriously <br />going to shield her? Enough noise.</p>
<p begin="00:08:49.120" end="00:08:54.640" style="s2">[screaming] My mentor&#39;s so cool. Come on,  </p>
<p begin="00:08:54.640" end="00:09:04.480" style="s2">apprentice. House Stormluff has too many <br />idiots to beat them all today. Okay.</p>
<p begin="00:09:04.480" end="00:09:17.520" style="s2">Housemaster Storm will return from private <br />training soon. This will not end quietly.</p>
<p begin="00:09:17.520" end="00:09:22.720" style="s2">Even a stray dog would leave this dump. <br />Please don&#39;t let this be my new house. Wait,  </p>
<p begin="00:09:22.720" end="00:09:28.400" style="s2">there&#39;s a ward under that illusion. Mento, <br />is this place hidden by a warding lattice?  </p>
<p begin="00:09:28.400" end="00:09:35.840" style="s2">Good eye. It&#39;s a veil ward maintained by your <br />third senior, Quinn. Only a keyed badge can  </p>
<p begin="00:09:35.840" end="00:09:42.560" style="s2">open it and reveal the real House Valiant. House <br />Valiant. If we&#39;re called Valiant, we must be the  </p>
<p begin="00:09:42.560" end="00:09:50.000" style="s2">strongest house at Astl, right? Officially, <br />this is House Valiant. I may have chosen the  </p>
<p begin="00:09:50.000" end="00:09:59.040" style="s2">name myself. Of course. Outside these gates, <br />you can apparently assign your own reputation.</p>
<p begin="00:09:59.040" end="00:10:02.720" style="s2">A housemaster locked out of her own <br />ward. How does that even happen?</p>
<p begin="00:10:05.600" end="00:10:12.640" style="s2">Quinn Mercer, [screaming] do you have any more <br />of those things you used to blow up the girl?  </p>
<p begin="00:10:12.640" end="00:10:23.840" style="s2">Thunder burst orbs. I have a few left. You call <br />this a few? Never mind. Aim there. Blast it.</p>
<p begin="00:10:23.840" end="00:10:30.640" style="s2">You threw all of them. Want me to keep going? <br />I still have a few. Those orbs can launch a  </p>
<p begin="00:10:30.640" end="00:10:36.160" style="s2">fourth rank blade caster. And she tosses <br />them like party poppers. I was right. This  </p>
<p begin="00:10:36.160" end="00:10:50.480" style="s2">girl&#39;s background is anything but ordinary. <br />Mentor, that&#39;s enough. No more blasting. Oh,</p>
<p begin="00:10:50.480" end="00:10:54.160" style="s2">now that&#39;s impressive.</p>
<p begin="00:10:54.160" end="00:10:56.560" style="s2">Let&#39;s go.</p>
<p begin="00:10:56.560" end="00:11:06.000" style="s2">[gasps and sighs]  </p>
<p begin="00:11:06.000" end="00:11:26.400" style="s2">All beautiful outside, empty <br />inside. This house is broke. mental.</p>
<p begin="00:11:26.400" end="00:11:32.000" style="s2">Mentor Leonard reporting in. <br />Okay, House Valiant may be broke,  </p>
<p begin="00:11:32.000" end="00:11:38.240" style="s2">but this guy is ridiculously handsome. Just <br />you. Where are the rest of those disasters?  </p>
<p begin="00:11:39.120" end="00:11:44.640" style="s2">Well, our second protege has been gone for <br />years. He&#39;s probably possibly hopefully still  </p>
<p begin="00:11:44.640" end="00:11:49.360" style="s2">alive. Quinn&#39;s even more jumpy than last <br />year. He&#39;s put 99 wards around his room,  </p>
<p begin="00:11:49.360" end="00:11:55.600" style="s2">so he probably didn&#39;t sense you were back. Um, <br />you know, Pers, unless his life or his money is  </p>
<p begin="00:11:55.600" end="00:12:02.000" style="s2">on the line, he won&#39;t budge. Leo and Julian were <br />both badly hurt sporing yesterday. They&#39;ve shut  </p>
<p begin="00:12:02.000" end="00:12:07.200" style="s2">themselves away to recover. So, out of my entire <br />house, you&#39;re the only one fit to show his face.</p>
<p begin="00:12:10.200" end="00:12:14.640" style="s2">[laughter] What did I do to deserve <br />this? Out of millions of students,  </p>
<p begin="00:12:14.640" end="00:12:20.480" style="s2">how did I pick every last one of these disasters?</p>
<p begin="00:12:20.480" end="00:12:26.880" style="s2">Thank the stars. I found one normal student <br />before House Valiant fell apart. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="00:12:26.880" end="00:12:31.520" style="s2">this is your senior, Leon. Nice to meet <br />you, Leon. I&#39;m Nina. I&#39;m a light magic. So,  </p>
<p begin="00:12:31.520" end="00:12:36.560" style="s2">you&#39;re our new junior. Here, <br />a welcome gift. It&#39;s an Aegus  </p>
<p begin="00:12:36.560" end="00:12:43.120" style="s2">cuff. A high-grade warding artifact. <br />It offers a little extra protection.</p>
<p begin="00:12:43.120" end="00:12:47.680" style="s2">High-grade. It looks about as sturdy <br />as the feed bowls back home. Thank you,  </p>
<p begin="00:12:47.680" end="00:12:54.080" style="s2">Leon. But gift should go both ways. <br />And I didn&#39;t exactly come prepared.</p>
<p begin="00:12:54.080" end="00:13:03.280" style="s2">You can have this. Is this storm struck wood <br />charged with an enormous amount of lightning  </p>
<p begin="00:13:03.280" end="00:13:09.680" style="s2">magic? 5,000-year-old storm struck wood. Do <br />you know how rare that is? And you turned it  </p>
<p begin="00:13:09.680" end="00:13:20.000" style="s2">into that. Nina, this is far too valuable. <br />I can&#39;t accept it. Don&#39;t worry. I have more.</p>
<p begin="00:13:20.000" end="00:13:28.960" style="s2">Mentor, this one&#39;s for you. 6,000-year-old <br />storm struck wood. You don&#39;t happen to have  </p>
<p begin="00:13:28.960" end="00:13:35.920" style="s2">just a tiny bit more of this stuff, do <br />you? Of course not. I knew it. This is  </p>
<p begin="00:13:35.920" end="00:13:53.440" style="s2">storm struck wood. No one has heaps of it <br />just lying around. I have mountains of it.</p>
<p begin="00:13:53.440" end="00:14:01.200" style="s2">Stormcrunt wood is priceless. Even a 3,000-year <br />piece could start a bidding war betweenmies. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="00:14:01.200" end="00:14:11.520" style="s2">you made a bowl out of it. What else <br />would I make? Don&#39;t you people eat?</p>
<p begin="00:14:11.520" end="00:14:18.400" style="s2">All right, put it away for now. Mentor, <br />everyone can use these. I have plenty more.</p>
<p begin="00:14:18.400" end="00:14:23.920" style="s2">That wood grows everywhere back <br />home. It really isn&#39;t rare.</p>
<p begin="00:14:23.920" end="00:14:28.880" style="s2">He hands out priceless treasures <br />like firewood. Who is this girl?  </p>
<p begin="00:14:29.520" end="00:14:36.960" style="s2">I really want to take it, but something <br />tells me I&#39;d die the second I tried.</p>
<p begin="00:14:36.960" end="00:14:41.600" style="s2">Do you know why I took you in? Because <br />I&#39;m the cutest person alive or because  </p>
<p begin="00:14:41.600" end="00:14:47.920" style="s2">you know I&#39;ll become the greatest healer in all <br />Astiful. [sighs] I took you in because Lyra,  </p>
<p begin="00:14:47.920" end="00:14:55.920" style="s2">when? Report to the Chancellor&#39;s Tower <br />immediately. Sooner than I expected.  </p>
<p begin="00:14:55.920" end="00:14:59.760" style="s2">Tell those disasters I don&#39;t care what <br />they did before. House Valiant is about  </p>
<p begin="00:14:59.760" end="00:15:08.320" style="s2">to be dissolved. I don&#39;t care how they do <br />it. They will prove they&#39;re not useless.</p>
<p begin="00:15:08.320" end="00:15:14.560" style="s2">Leon, what does she mean? House Valiant is being <br />dissolved. [sighs and gasps] I just got here. I  </p>
<p begin="00:15:14.560" end="00:15:22.480" style="s2">haven&#39;t even tasted a gale rabbit yet. And now <br />the whole house is closing. We failed her. Lyra  </p>
<p begin="00:15:22.480" end="00:15:26.240" style="s2">has seven bonded proteges, but none of us has <br />left the house grounds or entered an academy  </p>
<p begin="00:15:26.240" end="00:15:31.040" style="s2">trial in years. The council thinks House Valiant <br />serves no purpose, so they want it dissolved. Why  </p>
<p begin="00:15:31.040" end="00:15:47.520" style="s2">won&#39;t any of you leave? It&#39;s a long story. Come <br />on. Once you meet the others, you&#39;ll understand.</p>
<p begin="00:15:47.520" end="00:15:54.640" style="s2">House Valiant stays. Anyone who <br />disagrees can fight me for it. Enough,  </p>
