<p begin="00:31:39.920" end="00:31:46.560" style="s2">700?</p>
<p begin="00:31:46.560" end="00:31:53.040" style="s2">700. That&#39;s the threshold for a bonded <br />project. 700 in barely half an hour. Livia,  </p>
<p begin="00:31:53.040" end="00:32:02.240" style="s2">contact our mentor. A prodigy like this belongs <br />in House Storm Glass. 800. 800 at that speed.  </p>
<p begin="00:32:03.040" end="00:32:22.000" style="s2">A talent like this hasn&#39;t appeared in a century. <br />The chancellor must hear about it immediately.</p>
<p begin="00:32:22.000" end="00:32:27.920" style="s2">Lyra has gone too far. Recruiting a <br />student in the street was bad enough.</p>
<p begin="00:32:29.360" end="00:32:33.200" style="s2">She made the girl a bonded prodige before <br />she ever faced the thousandst step trial.  </p>
<p begin="00:32:33.200" end="00:32:38.480" style="s2">Do academy rules mean nothing to her? The <br />rules require 700 steps. Nina is a third  </p>
<p begin="00:32:38.480" end="00:32:43.520" style="s2">wrangle light mage. Reaching 200 would be a <br />miracle. By forcing her into the trial now,  </p>
<p begin="00:32:43.520" end="00:32:47.440" style="s2">Lyra is practically demanding that <br />we falsify the result. This isn&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="00:32:47.440" end="00:32:54.480" style="s2">mentorship. Lyra is trading on her old <br />reputation to defy academy law in public.</p>
<p begin="00:32:55.840" end="00:33:05.440" style="s2">Chancellor, someone cleared 800. No, 900 steps.</p>
<p begin="00:33:05.440" end="00:33:21.920" style="s2">900.</p>
<p begin="00:33:21.920" end="00:33:28.160" style="s2">Chancellor, the prodigy has reached 950.</p>
<p begin="00:33:28.160" end="00:33:33.120" style="s2">Chancellor, a talent like this appears once in <br />a century. I volunteer to make this student my  </p>
<p begin="00:33:33.120" end="00:33:38.640" style="s2">personal protege and teach them everything <br />I know. Not so fast, Southwell. A will this  </p>
<p begin="00:33:38.640" end="00:33:44.800" style="s2">strong perfectly suits my discipline. I should <br />be the one to train this student. Enough. If  </p>
<p begin="00:33:44.800" end="00:33:49.600" style="s2">this student reaches the summit, I will take <br />them as my own protege and raise them as Avel  </p>
<p begin="00:33:49.600" end="00:34:01.760" style="s2">Academyy&#39;s successor. What are you all fighting <br />over? This prodigy is already my student.</p>
<p begin="00:34:01.760" end="00:34:07.520" style="s2">You&#39;re not talking about Nenina, that little <br />light mage, are you? A third rank light mage  </p>
<p begin="00:34:07.520" end="00:34:13.120" style="s2">had climbed 950 steps in less than an hour. <br />I know you want to defend your student,  </p>
<p begin="00:34:13.120" end="00:34:18.400" style="s2">Housemaster Win, but that&#39;s an outrageous lie.</p>
<p begin="00:34:19.280" end="00:34:23.280" style="s2">Leon tells me you already made a bet with my <br />student. What? Do you want to make another  </p>
<p begin="00:34:23.280" end="00:34:32.160" style="s2">one with me? What are the stakes? Your frost <br />bloom. If you lose, I take the blade. If I lose,  </p>
<p begin="00:34:32.160" end="00:34:39.360" style="s2">this soul pel, a legendary grade artifact, is <br />yours. Deal. But I have one more condition. If  </p>
<p begin="00:34:39.360" end="00:34:48.400" style="s2">you lose, you cannot interfere when I kill Nina. <br />Agreed. Livia, Frost Bloom is one of Astallur&#39;s  </p>
<p begin="00:34:48.400" end="00:34:55.440" style="s2">greatest relics. Our mentor fought hard to <br />obtain it. Are you sure you should wager it?  </p>
<p begin="00:34:55.440" end="00:35:01.440" style="s2">Don&#39;t worry. Nina can&#39;t possibly reach 950. <br />I&#39;ll get to kill her and I&#39;ll win the soul  </p>
<p begin="00:35:01.440" end="00:35:09.600" style="s2">bell our mentor has always wanted. Housem when <br />please reconsider. Nina is only a third ranked  </p>
<p begin="00:35:09.600" end="00:35:14.800" style="s2">light mage and a brand new student. Wagering <br />a legendary grade artifact on her is reckless.  </p>
<p begin="00:35:15.360" end="00:35:30.320" style="s2">Don&#39;t worry, they&#39;re the only ones who can lose.</p>
<p begin="00:35:30.320" end="00:35:36.560" style="s2">Watch out. She found the hidden step. <br />She reached the true summit. In all  </p>
<p begin="00:35:36.560" end="00:35:39.280" style="s2">of Astal Academyy&#39;s history, <br />no one has ever reached the  </p>
<p begin="00:35:39.280" end="00:35:55.280" style="s2">true summit. Not one person. It&#39;s her. <br />The light made it. Nina Rowan. Nina.</p>
<p begin="00:35:55.280" end="00:36:01.520" style="s2">Impossible. A third ranked light mage cannot <br />reach the true summit. She must have cheated.  </p>
<p begin="00:36:01.520" end="00:36:09.360" style="s2">Exactly. She cheated. The result is invalid. <br />The chancellor will decide whether it counts,  </p>
<p begin="00:36:09.360" end="00:36:19.120" style="s2">but our wager is due. Frost Bloom, hand it over.</p>
<p begin="00:36:19.120" end="00:36:25.520" style="s2">The Thunder Trial. The True Summit has opened <br />the Thunder Trial. [gasps] Even a fifth rank  </p>
<p begin="00:36:25.520" end="00:36:31.840" style="s2">body major might not survive that ordeal. She&#39;s <br />only third rank and a light pagist at that. I&#39;m  </p>
<p begin="00:36:31.840" end="00:36:36.400" style="s2">afraid she won&#39;t make it out alive. That&#39;s what <br />she gets for cheating. I hope the lightning  </p>
<p begin="00:36:36.400" end="00:36:42.720" style="s2">burns her to ash. This saves us the trouble. We <br />won&#39;t have to lift a finger. The thunder will  </p>
<p begin="00:36:42.720" end="00:36:47.600" style="s2">erasate her for us. How could a light magent <br />survive that lightning? That poor girl is as  </p>
<p begin="00:36:47.600" end="00:36:52.240" style="s2">good as dead. That&#39;s what happens when you <br />fake strength you don&#39;t have. She cheated,  </p>
<p begin="00:36:52.240" end="00:37:00.720" style="s2">failed, and threw away her <br />life. Nina, please be all right.</p>
<p begin="00:37:00.720" end="00:37:04.880" style="s2">I thought there were only 999 steps. <br />Where did the thousandth come from? And  </p>
<p begin="00:37:04.880" end="00:37:08.720" style="s2">what are those clouds doing? Don&#39;t <br />tell me that lightning is for me.</p>
<p begin="00:37:14.560" end="00:37:21.280" style="s2">It really is striking me.</p>
<p begin="00:37:21.280" end="00:37:31.120" style="s2">Come on then. Is that all <br />you&#39;ve got? Hit me again.</p>
<p begin="00:37:38.240" end="00:37:42.640" style="s2">She&#39;s dead. Housemaster win, your precious <br />student was struck dead. That&#39;s what cheaters  </p>
<p begin="00:37:42.640" end="00:37:48.080" style="s2">deserve. What an easy death. Trash is still <br />trash. She cheated her way to the top and  </p>
<p begin="00:37:48.080" end="00:37:53.280" style="s2">still couldn&#39;t survive it. The first student <br />in academy history to reach the true summit  </p>
<p begin="00:37:53.280" end="00:38:03.520" style="s2">lost to the thunder trial. What a waste. <br />Meant to look. Nina opened her eyes. What?</p>
<p begin="00:38:03.520" end="00:38:08.000" style="s2">That&#39;s it. Two strikes.</p>
<p begin="00:38:08.000" end="00:38:18.600" style="s2">I was expecting 10 at least. I waited all that <br />time for nothing. Done. Time for more Gail Rabbit.</p>
<p begin="00:38:18.600" end="00:38:32.000" style="s2">[gasps] Are you hurt? Nina, does anything feel <br />wrong? I&#39;m fine. Every strike hit my blade case.  </p>
<p begin="00:38:32.000" end="00:38:40.080" style="s2">I didn&#39;t feel a thing. Clever girl. She survived <br />even that stubborn little freak. Reckless child.  </p>
<p begin="00:38:40.080" end="00:38:43.840" style="s2">Do you have any idea what you just wasted? <br />That was the storm forging trial. An archonic  </p>
<p begin="00:38:43.840" end="00:38:47.120" style="s2">strengthening right that appears once in a <br />thousand years. And you let your blade case block  </p>
<p begin="00:38:47.120" end="00:38:51.760" style="s2">every strike. Storm forging? I don&#39;t need it. My <br />fathers have trained me with lightning since I  </p>
<p begin="00:38:51.760" end="00:38:58.160" style="s2">was little. There&#39;s nothing left for the trial to <br />strengthen. Enough. She&#39;s young. She didn&#39;t know.  </p>
<p begin="00:38:58.160" end="00:39:02.640" style="s2">But reaching the true summit makes her a once <br />in a centured talent. Neil, Nina, I will take  </p>
<p begin="00:39:02.640" end="00:39:19.840" style="s2">you as my personal protege. Nina. Neil. This is <br />Chancellor Shaw. He almost never takes a student.</p>
<p begin="00:39:19.840" end="00:39:24.960" style="s2">I already have a mentor. I&#39;m not kneeling.</p>
<p begin="00:39:24.960" end="00:39:30.080" style="s2">That&#39;s my girl. Another eccentric <br />house. Valiant really does collect  </p>
<p begin="00:39:30.080" end="00:39:34.640" style="s2">them. My student reached the summit, so <br />it&#39;s time to settle our wager. Frostbloom,  </p>
<p begin="00:39:34.640" end="00:39:41.040" style="s2">will you hand it over or shall I take it myself?</p>
<p begin="00:39:41.040" end="00:39:47.280" style="s2">Saurin, our mentor gave me Frost Bloom <br />herself. It&#39;s my bonded blade. Housem Win,  </p>
<p begin="00:39:47.280" end="00:39:49.600" style="s2">Frost Bloom was our mentor&#39;s gift to Livia. You&#39;re  </p>
<p begin="00:39:49.600" end="00:39:55.440" style="s2">the head of a great house. Aren&#39;t you <br />ashamed to take a student&#39;s possession?</p>
<p begin="00:40:00.000" end="00:40:08.400" style="s2">A wager is a wager. She agreed to the <br />terms. Now she lives with the result.</p>
<p begin="00:40:08.400" end="00:40:12.720" style="s2">This blade is nice and cold. Leon, what&#39;s <br />going on? While you were in the trial,  </p>
<p begin="00:40:12.720" end="00:40:22.000" style="s2">Mena made another bet with Livia. If you reach the <br />summit, Frost Bloom is yours. Oh, so it&#39;s free.</p>
<p begin="00:40:23.920" end="00:40:29.600" style="s2">That&#39;s my blade. You&#39;re a light mage. What <br />could you possibly do with it? Nothing,  </p>
<p begin="00:40:29.600" end="00:40:37.120" style="s2">really. But summer&#39;s coming. It&#39;ll be nice for <br />keeping cool. Free is free. Thanks. Chancellor  </p>
<p begin="00:40:37.120" end="00:40:40.880" style="s2">of Frostbloom was a personal gift from my <br />mentor. Couldn&#39;t you? She lost the wager.  </p>
<p begin="00:40:40.880" end="00:40:48.480" style="s2">I will not interfere. Wait, you&#39;re leaving <br />already? Aren&#39;t you forgetting something?  </p>
<p begin="00:40:48.480" end="00:40:54.480" style="s2">You promised to kneel and apologize if I <br />cleared 700. I reached the true summit. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="00:40:54.480" end="00:40:59.920" style="s2">enough. Livia already gave you her bonded <br />blade. What more do you want? Saurin, your  </p>
<p begin="00:40:59.920" end="00:41:04.240" style="s2">junior has threatened to kill Nina over and over. <br />Minutes ago, she was celebrating when she thought  </p>
<p begin="00:41:04.240" end="00:41:11.600" style="s2">lightning had killed her. Nina is only asking <br />for the apology she was promised. That&#39;s mercy.</p>
<p begin="00:41:11.600" end="00:41:17.840" style="s2">Apologize.</p>
<p begin="00:41:17.840" end="00:41:36.080" style="s2">I&#39;m sorry. What was that? I couldn&#39;t <br />hear you. I&#39;m sorry. Much better.</p>
<p begin="00:41:36.080" end="00:41:40.640" style="s2">Nina, this isn&#39;t over. Someday I&#39;ll <br />repay today&#39;s humiliation a hundfold.  </p>
<p begin="00:41:40.640" end="00:41:47.040" style="s2">You humiliated Livia. One day I&#39;ll <br />teach you what regret feels like.</p>
<p begin="00:41:49.520" end="00:41:53.840" style="s2">Mentor Leon, I climbed a thousand steps.  </p>
<p begin="00:41:53.840" end="00:42:01.840" style="s2">I&#39;m starving. Where&#39;s the gale <br />rabbit you promised? [laughter]</p>
<p begin="00:42:01.840" end="00:42:11.680" style="s2">Food? That&#39;s all you think about? Come on. Pierce <br />is an incredible cook. We&#39;ll make him feed you.</p>
<p begin="00:42:19.120" end="00:42:21.920" style="s2">Nina, this rabbit feast cost me <br />6 months worth of activity. You  </p>
<p begin="00:42:21.920" end="00:42:28.480" style="s2">promised me a way to get rich without <br />lifting a finger. So, let&#39;s hear it.</p>
<p begin="00:42:28.480" end="00:42:34.480" style="s2">Not spicy enough. Understood. More heat coming up.</p>
<p begin="00:42:34.480" end="00:42:39.360" style="s2">The academy looks down on House Valiant because no <br />one enters competitions. That&#39;s why we&#39;re facing  </p>
<p begin="00:42:39.360" end="00:42:45.520" style="s2">dissolution. If I can get Pierce to volunteer for <br />one match, maybe I can break the crisis. Pier,  </p>
<p begin="00:42:45.520" end="00:42:54.560" style="s2">you&#39;ve been here all these years. Have you <br />ever fought in the Arcane League Arena?</p>
<p begin="00:42:54.560" end="00:42:59.120" style="s2">Why would I? Fighting makes you sweaty, and <br />sweating is exhausting. I&#39;d rather catch up  </p>
<p begin="00:42:59.120" end="00:43:04.560" style="s2">on my beauty sleep. Every Arcane League match <br />takes wages. Everyone thinks House Valiant is  </p>
<p begin="00:43:04.560" end="00:43:09.040" style="s2">full of weaklings. Challenge one of Astallur&#39;s <br />most popular fighters and they&#39;ll assume you&#39;re  </p>
<p begin="00:43:09.040" end="00:43:23.520" style="s2">certain to lose. Your odds will sore. Then <br />you bet on yourself. And I make a fortune.</p>
<p begin="00:43:23.520" end="00:43:29.360" style="s2">Nina, you&#39;re brilliant. How did you <br />dream up something this perfect? I  </p>
<p begin="00:43:29.360" end="00:43:35.640" style="s2">was born brilliant. She&#39;s even more <br />adorable than I expected. [snorts]</p>
<p begin="00:43:39.440" end="00:43:47.520" style="s2">My mentor gave me that blade herself and Nina and <br />took it. Then she made me kneel and apologize.  </p>
<p begin="00:43:47.520" end="00:43:52.080" style="s2">How will students from the other houses look at <br />me now? How am I supposed to face anyone at the  </p>
<p begin="00:43:52.080" end="00:44:00.400" style="s2">academy now? Don&#39;t cry. When our mentor returns, <br />he&#39;ll find you an even better blade. As for Nina,  </p>
<p begin="00:44:00.400" end="00:44:06.880" style="s2">she&#39;s only a third ranked light magist. <br />I&#39;ll find a chance to kill her myself.</p>
<p begin="00:44:06.880" end="00:44:16.080" style="s2">You promise? I swear. When <br />have I ever lied to you?</p>
<p begin="00:44:16.080" end="00:44:28.800" style="s2">Saurin Pierce Bellicanin, House Valiant&#39;s fourth <br />protege, just challenged you to a match. What?</p>
<p begin="00:44:31.280" end="00:44:35.040" style="s2">Where is Pierce? The match should <br />have started already. Did he lose  </p>
<p begin="00:44:35.040" end="00:44:42.480" style="s2">his nerve? No one from House Valiant has <br />competed in years. He probably issued the  </p>
<p begin="00:44:42.480" end="00:44:48.480" style="s2">challenge for attention and never intended <br />to show. They hold bonded protege seats and  </p>
<p begin="00:44:48.480" end="00:44:56.320" style="s2">contribute nothing. House Valiant should <br />have been dissolved years ago. Exactly.</p>
<p begin="00:44:59.600" end="00:45:06.240" style="s2">Livia, the council has issued a dissolution <br />order against House Valiant. If no one from  </p>
<p begin="00:45:06.240" end="00:45:15.040" style="s2">the house enters and wins a match before the <br />deadline, the house will be erased for good.</p>
<p begin="00:45:15.040" end="00:45:26.000" style="s2">Perfect. Once Nina loses her bonded status, <br />no one can stop me from killing her.</p>
<p begin="00:45:26.000" end="00:45:37.520" style="s2">There, Pierce is here.</p>
<p begin="00:45:37.520" end="00:45:42.080" style="s2">Piers Bellabby, you actually showed up. You talk  </p>
<p begin="00:45:42.080" end="00:45:46.000" style="s2">too much. Let&#39;s get this over <br />with. I have a nap to finish.</p>
<p begin="00:45:54.080" end="00:45:59.360" style="s2">Put all of it on peels.</p>
<p begin="00:45:59.360" end="00:46:07.760" style="s2">All these crystals. Are you sure? Saurin is one of <br />Astal&#39;s top 10 prodigies. I&#39;m sure House Valiant  </p>
<p begin="00:46:07.760" end="00:46:14.960" style="s2">doesn&#39;t lose. All right, your wager is registered. <br />My bet&#39;s on Saurin. Same here and mine.  </p>
<p begin="00:46:16.240" end="00:46:21.360" style="s2">Saurin, crush that man for me.</p>
<p begin="00:46:21.360" end="00:46:28.720" style="s2">Relax. He&#39;s never fought a real match. <br />I&#39;ll teach him the meaning of regret.</p>
<p begin="00:46:28.720" end="00:46:34.960" style="s2">Go, P. I bet every one of <br />your ether crystals on you.</p>
<p begin="00:46:34.960" end="00:46:41.680" style="s2">Don&#39;t worry. For my crystals, I refuse to lose.</p>
<p begin="00:46:56.400" end="00:47:04.640" style="s2">Sarin Hail of House Storm Glass <br />versus Pier Bella of House Valiant.</p>
<p begin="00:47:04.640" end="00:47:08.240" style="s2">Begin.</p>
<p begin="00:47:16.400" end="00:47:25.920" style="s2">A dumb beast thinks it can stop me. <br />Snowy Shade, you join in, too. Shade,  </p>
<p begin="00:47:25.920" end="00:47:30.320" style="s2">there&#39;s another Ark and Familiar. Where? <br />I don&#39;t see anything. He&#39;s bluffing.  </p>
<p begin="00:47:30.320" end="00:47:37.680" style="s2">It&#39;s adorable. I want to pet it so badly. But <br />Shade is right there. Can no one else see it?</p>
<p begin="00:47:42.480" end="00:47:54.960" style="s2">cheap tricks. Blazing Ark.</p>
<p begin="00:47:54.960" end="00:48:04.640" style="s2">It appears I&#39;ve won. The match is over. <br />Pier Bellamman of House Valiant wins.  </p>
<p begin="00:48:04.640" end="00:48:09.760" style="s2">My crystals. I bet an entire month&#39;s <br />allowance on Saurin. Who said everyone  </p>
<p begin="00:48:09.760" end="00:48:15.920" style="s2">in House Valiion was useless? Show <br />yourself. I promise I won&#39;t kill you.</p>
<p begin="00:48:15.920" end="00:48:22.880" style="s2">[sighs] I didn&#39;t lose. You caught <br />me off guard. That&#39;s all. Fields,  </p>
<p begin="00:48:22.880" end="00:48:33.040" style="s2">don&#39;t think I&#39;m afraid of you. If <br />you have the nerve, fight me again.</p>
<p begin="00:48:42.000" end="00:48:48.800" style="s2">You&#39;re saying if I throw the next <br />match, the odds will climb even higher.</p>
<p begin="00:48:48.800" end="00:48:51.200" style="s2">Fine. If you can&#39;t accept the result,  </p>
<p begin="00:48:51.200" end="00:48:59.840" style="s2">we&#39;ll go again. This time, I won&#39;t <br />give you a chance to ambush me.</p>
<p begin="00:48:59.840" end="00:49:08.960" style="s2">Pers. Everything on Pier. I was blind <br />before. I&#39;m not losing twice. Me, too.</p>
<p begin="00:49:08.960" end="00:49:17.600" style="s2">Pier can&#39;t lose. I&#39;m betting on Pits, too.</p>
<p begin="00:49:17.600" end="00:49:23.760" style="s2">Livia, you too.</p>
<p begin="00:49:23.760" end="00:49:28.400" style="s2">It&#39;s not that I don&#39;t believe in you. You&#39;re hurt.  </p>
