<p begin="01:05:54.000" end="01:06:20.560" style="s2">Looks like it&#39;s time to draw my <br />blades. Scarlet, Amber, you&#39;re up.</p>
<p begin="01:06:20.560" end="01:06:25.440" style="s2">I haven&#39;t even drawn my blades. Who did that? No.</p>
<p begin="01:06:28.320" end="01:06:33.200" style="s2">You shattered their magic <br />cores. Nina, you&#39;re dead. So,  </p>
<p begin="01:06:33.200" end="01:06:39.520" style="s2">you&#39;re allowed to kill me, but <br />no one&#39;s allowed to fight back.</p>
<p begin="01:06:39.520" end="01:06:46.320" style="s2">Enough.</p>
<p begin="01:06:46.320" end="01:06:50.960" style="s2">Victor was at fault. Matriarch. She destroyed  </p>
<p begin="01:06:50.960" end="01:06:54.880" style="s2">our family ward and shattered <br />both my senior&#39;s magic cores.</p>
<p begin="01:06:58.000" end="01:07:07.840" style="s2">I said Victor was at fault. Finally, someone <br />reasonable. Girl, Victor and Serena harmed  </p>
<p begin="01:07:07.840" end="01:07:11.840" style="s2">your mother. You have every right to hate <br />him. But the rest of the family truly knew  </p>
<p begin="01:07:11.840" end="01:07:16.000" style="s2">nothing. You&#39;ve blown up our ward and <br />wrecked our home. What if we end this  </p>
<p begin="01:07:16.000" end="01:07:23.840" style="s2">here? Fine. On two conditions. First, return <br />every enchanted item from my mother&#39;s dowy.</p>
<p begin="01:07:29.280" end="01:07:36.240" style="s2">Second, I want Victor to kneel before <br />my mother&#39;s memorial and apologize.</p>
<p begin="01:07:36.240" end="01:07:50.160" style="s2">Kneel to her. Never. Silence.</p>
<p begin="01:07:50.160" end="01:07:52.800" style="s2">Neil.</p>
<p begin="01:07:55.840" end="01:08:03.200" style="s2">I was wrong. I&#39;m guilty. I wronged you and <br />our daughter. Shame my mother couldn&#39;t see  </p>
<p begin="01:08:03.200" end="01:08:09.280" style="s2">it herself. You heard him. Your father <br />is guilty. Spread another lie about me  </p>
<p begin="01:08:09.280" end="01:08:19.120" style="s2">and boom. Next time I won&#39;t bother with <br />witness mirrors. I&#39;ll use explosive.</p>
<p begin="01:08:19.120" end="01:08:22.320" style="s2">The witness mirrors stay up until they <br />run out of crystals. Don&#39;t touch them.  </p>
<p begin="01:08:22.320" end="01:08:30.400" style="s2">Take one down and I&#39;ll put <br />up two more. I have plenty.</p>
<p begin="01:08:30.400" end="01:08:33.520" style="s2">From today on, Veale descendants will guard the  </p>
<p begin="01:08:33.520" end="01:08:42.560" style="s2">witness mirrors in shifts. <br />Not one is to be damaged.</p>
<p begin="01:08:42.560" end="01:08:48.640" style="s2">Come out. You&#39;ve helped me this whole <br />way. Aren&#39;t you going to show yourself?</p>
<p begin="01:08:57.600" end="01:09:02.960" style="s2">Wow, he&#39;s gorgeous. Don&#39;t tell me he&#39;s <br />another one of my seniors. Ian Blake,  </p>
<p begin="01:09:02.960" end="01:09:07.120" style="s2">House Valiant&#39;s sixth protetéé. <br />Nice to meet you, Nina. Wait,  </p>
<p begin="01:09:07.120" end="01:09:14.560" style="s2">sixth? I&#39;ve had this nagging feeling I <br />forgot something. I forgot an entire senior.</p>
<p begin="01:09:14.560" end="01:09:19.440" style="s2">You helped me at the Veil Estate, didn&#39;t <br />you? Thank you. But did you just return  </p>
<p begin="01:09:19.440" end="01:09:24.080" style="s2">to the academy and happen to see me? No, I was in <br />close training at House Valiant and only returned  </p>
<p begin="01:09:24.080" end="01:09:31.680" style="s2">recently. Leon said you needed protection, so <br />I came. But Leon and the others never mentioned  </p>
<p begin="01:09:31.680" end="01:09:38.320" style="s2">that House Valiant had a sixth prodigge. They <br />probably forgot. My discipline minimizes my  </p>
<p begin="01:09:38.320" end="01:09:45.520" style="s2">presence. Even my own housemates often forget I <br />exist. That&#39;s an incredible discipline. Right,  </p>
<p begin="01:09:45.520" end="01:09:51.200" style="s2">I need to go to the Grand Archive. Ian, I&#39;ll <br />come find you when I get back. Assuming she still  </p>
<p begin="01:09:51.200" end="01:09:59.440" style="s2">remembers me. Didn&#39;t I tell you to collect the <br />companion manual yourself? Why are you back? No,  </p>
<p begin="01:09:59.440" end="01:10:04.320" style="s2">wait. Did you get your head caught in a door? <br />I&#39;m just a gatekeeper. Why do you keep bringing  </p>
<p begin="01:10:04.320" end="01:10:10.080" style="s2">me wine? I don&#39;t have any real authority. In <br />every story, the harmless old caretaker is a  </p>
<p begin="01:10:10.080" end="01:10:14.720" style="s2">secret master. You can&#39;t go wrong bringing an <br />archment wine. You&#39;re overthinking it. I have  </p>
<p begin="01:10:14.720" end="01:10:24.720" style="s2">so much of this wine, it just takes up space <br />in my storage pouch. You may as well have it.</p>
<p begin="01:10:24.720" end="01:10:27.920" style="s2">Sir, have you heard of backfiring <br />healing? The kind where a healing  </p>
<p begin="01:10:27.920" end="01:10:39.920" style="s2">spell makes an injury worse? No, never. Get out,</p>
<p begin="01:10:39.920" end="01:10:45.840" style="s2">brat. still much more likable than <br />that little menaced Lyra. Chancellor,  </p>
<p begin="01:10:45.840" end="01:10:51.680" style="s2">Nenah left the academy without permission, <br />stormed my home, destroyed our family ward,  </p>
<p begin="01:10:51.680" end="01:11:01.440" style="s2">and had an outsider shatter both my senior&#39;s <br />magic cores. Please give us justice.</p>
<p begin="01:11:01.440" end="01:11:08.240" style="s2">I&#39;ve been informed. Livia, leave for now. Take <br />those two students to the infirmary. Chancellor  </p>
<p begin="01:11:08.240" end="01:11:16.400" style="s2">Nina conspired with an outsider to shatter both my <br />seniors as magic cause and you&#39;re letting it go.</p>
<p begin="01:11:16.400" end="01:11:22.320" style="s2">Arch Mace, since you&#39;re here, show yourself. You <br />understood that message, didn&#39;t you? Those two  </p>
<p begin="01:11:22.320" end="01:11:27.200" style="s2">brats with shattered cause attacked Nina first. <br />You can punish her, but then both sides get the  </p>
<p begin="01:11:27.200" end="01:11:31.360" style="s2">same sentence. Even if both sides share blame, <br />what about the outsider who attacked them from  </p>
<p begin="01:11:31.360" end="01:11:38.560" style="s2">the shadows? Whoever dares attack Aville&#39;s <br />students must pay. Then punish him. No  </p>
<p begin="01:11:38.560" end="01:11:46.880" style="s2">need to search. The one who injured them is an <br />astrophall student too. An astrophall student.</p>
<p begin="01:11:46.880" end="01:11:51.760" style="s2">House valiant. Interesting young man. Still, <br />he was too ruthless with fellow students. He  </p>
<p begin="01:11:51.760" end="01:11:56.160" style="s2">should be punished. Those storm glass fools have <br />acted like they&#39;ve lost their minds ever since  </p>
<p begin="01:11:56.160" end="01:12:00.800" style="s2">the veil girl enrolled. One word from her and they <br />tried to murder a fellow student. What is Luke and  </p>
<p begin="01:12:00.800" end="01:12:05.760" style="s2">Stormmy teaching them? When he returns, you need <br />to set him straight. I&#39;ve heard what happened in  </p>
<p begin="01:12:05.760" end="01:12:13.200" style="s2">High Court. News travels fast, Leon. [sighs and <br />gasps] No wonder you didn&#39;t need our help. Your  </p>
<p begin="01:12:13.200" end="01:12:23.120" style="s2">enchanted items handled everything. Only your <br />fortune could sustain a spectacle like that.</p>
<p begin="01:12:23.120" end="01:12:28.240" style="s2">House Valiant&#39;s first protetéé Leon Arden, <br />sixth protetéé Ian Blake, and eighth protetéé  </p>
<p begin="01:12:28.240" end="01:12:37.440" style="s2">Nina Rowan report to the Chancellor&#39;s Hall at <br />once. I knew I was forgetting something. Ian.</p>
<p begin="01:12:37.440" end="01:12:40.800" style="s2">Now I remember. Ian came back and told me <br />what happened in High Court. I remembered  </p>
<p begin="01:12:40.800" end="01:12:44.560" style="s2">the story and forgot the man. House <br />Storm Lamb reported us the moment  </p>
<p begin="01:12:44.560" end="01:12:49.680" style="s2">they returned. Doesn&#39;t matter. I didn&#39;t do <br />anything wrong. Exactly. No one from House  </p>
<p begin="01:12:49.680" end="01:12:58.640" style="s2">Valiant takes an injustice lying down. Come <br />on. We&#39;re going to the Chancellor&#39;s Tower.</p>
<p begin="01:12:58.640" end="01:13:04.080" style="s2">Nina, you left the academy without permission. <br />destroyed the Veil family ward and sent someone  </p>
<p begin="01:13:04.080" end="01:13:09.520" style="s2">to shatter my storm glass students magic course. <br />Do you admit your crimes? Victor Vale murdered  </p>
<p begin="01:13:09.520" end="01:13:15.040" style="s2">my birth mother, then spread lies to sneak me. <br />I destroyed the Veil ward to get justice. What  </p>
<p begin="01:13:15.040" end="01:13:20.720" style="s2">crime did I commit? Even if you had cause? <br />What about sending someone to shatter the  </p>
<p begin="01:13:20.720" end="01:13:25.840" style="s2">magic cause of my house&#39;s properties? You still <br />deny that? So when your storm glassass properties  </p>
<p begin="01:13:25.840" end="01:13:29.840" style="s2">try to kill me for no reason, a light agent who <br />can&#39;t beat them isn&#39;t allowed to ask for help,  </p>
<p begin="01:13:29.840" end="01:13:34.960" style="s2">I should just stand there and let them cut <br />me down. You, [clears throat] Deep Cole,  </p>
<p begin="01:13:34.960" end="01:13:39.520" style="s2">why did the Storm Glass Prophetes attack first? <br />They were defending a fellow student. And even so,  </p>
<p begin="01:13:39.520" end="01:13:45.280" style="s2">your side had no right to be so brutal and shatter <br />their cause. Nina wasn&#39;t the one who struck them,  </p>
<p begin="01:13:45.280" end="01:13:50.720" style="s2">and Stormlass attacked first. Chancellor, even if <br />Nenah didn&#39;t do it herself, it had to be someone  </p>
<p begin="01:13:50.720" end="01:13:56.160" style="s2">she knows. That person harmed Astall Proteiges. <br />The penalty should be death. Students who fight  </p>
<p begin="01:13:56.160" end="01:14:01.440" style="s2">in private should be punished. But an outsider <br />crippled Astal Proteis. We cannot let that pass.  </p>
<p begin="01:14:01.440" end="01:14:06.080" style="s2">Exactly. [clears throat] I nearly forgot again. <br />The person who hurt the Stormlass Peudles wasn&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="01:14:06.080" end="01:14:16.080" style="s2">an outsider. It was Ian Blake, House Valiant&#39;s <br />sixth pretier. Didn&#39;t I tell you two to bring him?</p>
<p begin="01:14:16.080" end="01:14:21.120" style="s2">We left in such a hurry. I forgot to tell <br />Ian. Don&#39;t feel guilty, Leon. I&#39;m used to it.  </p>
<p begin="01:14:21.120" end="01:14:29.280" style="s2">Why does that make me feel even worse? You <br />attacked the storm glass students? I did. You dare  </p>
<p begin="01:14:29.280" end="01:14:35.840" style="s2">moan fellow students? The nerve. It wasn&#39;t maming <br />for its own sake. Nina would have died under  </p>
<p begin="01:14:35.840" end="01:14:40.240" style="s2">their blades if I hadn&#39;t intervened. It was an <br />emergency. Of course, I couldn&#39;t control my force  </p>
<p begin="01:14:40.240" end="01:14:45.040" style="s2">perfectly. Does anyone actually think Stormlass <br />protetes are all so pathetic that my senior could  </p>
<p begin="01:14:45.040" end="01:14:55.520" style="s2">fight twoon-one and still hold back? You dare <br />insult House Storm Glass like this? Go enough.</p>
<p begin="01:14:55.520" end="01:15:00.160" style="s2">I&#39;ve reached a decision.</p>
<p begin="01:15:00.160" end="01:15:06.320" style="s2">House Storm Glass attacked first. House Valant <br />responded. Both sides are at faults. All five  </p>
<p begin="01:15:06.320" end="01:15:10.320" style="s2">students involved will serve two months <br />of watch duty at Ember Rich. The two with  </p>
<p begin="01:15:10.320" end="01:15:15.840" style="s2">damaged cores will repair them here and serve <br />their terms after recovery. Any objections?  </p>
<p begin="01:15:15.840" end="01:15:23.360" style="s2">A fair ruling, Chancellor. Chancellor, Livia <br />never attacked anyone. Nina Lee blew her up  </p>
<p begin="01:15:23.360" end="01:15:28.240" style="s2">instead. She&#39;s already devastated over our <br />two juniors. She can&#39;t endure Ember Rift.  </p>
<p begin="01:15:28.240" end="01:15:34.880" style="s2">Let me serve her sentence. Saurin, mind yourself. <br />Are you telling me how to do my job? I wouldn&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="01:15:34.880" end="01:15:44.400" style="s2">dare. Livia is truly innocent. Solen, in that <br />case, you can serve the sentence with her.</p>
<p begin="01:15:44.400" end="01:15:48.480" style="s2">Leon, what is Ember Rift? Why was <br />Livia so terrified? Below Ember Rift  </p>
<p begin="01:15:48.480" end="01:15:51.920" style="s2">is a natural sea of fire. Legend says <br />several rare flames are hidden inside,  </p>
<p begin="01:15:51.920" end="01:15:55.280" style="s2">though no one&#39;s ever found them. The heat <br />is brutal and conditions are harsh, but the  </p>
<p begin="01:15:55.280" end="01:16:00.720" style="s2">volcano hasn&#39;t stirred in a century. Mostly, it&#39;s <br />quiet, miserable duty. Deep within Ember Rift,  </p>
<p begin="01:16:00.720" end="01:16:06.560" style="s2">an extremely dangerous man is sealed. Nyxar, the <br />Beast King. They say his power is immeasurable.  </p>
<p begin="01:16:06.560" end="01:16:10.560" style="s2">Several senior faculty joined forces to <br />imprison him beneath the fire 10 years ago.  </p>
<p begin="01:16:10.560" end="01:16:15.440" style="s2">The seal has never weakened, but standing <br />watch there still carries some risk. The  </p>
<p begin="01:16:15.440" end="01:16:29.264" style="s2">seal&#39;s held for 10 years. It can&#39;t possibly fail <br />the moment I arrive. You alone at Ember Ridge.</p>
<p begin="01:16:29.264" end="01:16:38.880" style="s2">[clears throat] You and Ian be careful.</p>
<p begin="01:16:38.880" end="01:16:45.040" style="s2">Nina. Ian, why are you following me? <br />Oh, right. We&#39;re serving the sentence  </p>
<p begin="01:16:45.040" end="01:16:53.280" style="s2">together. Storm Glass hasn&#39;t arrived <br />yet. Let&#39;s choose our quarters first.</p>
<p begin="01:16:53.280" end="01:16:57.840" style="s2">We only need to check the rift every 4 hours. <br />The rest of the time, we can stay here and  </p>
<p begin="01:16:57.840" end="01:17:07.440" style="s2">train. Got it. Ian, these are frost fruits. One <br />will keep the heat off for 2 or 3 days. Here.  </p>
<p begin="01:17:07.440" end="01:17:17.680" style="s2">How does Nina have everything? Thank you. If <br />you ever need anything, come to me. I will.</p>
<p begin="01:17:17.680" end="01:17:20.880" style="s2">Livia, this is as far as we go. It&#39;s so <br />hot. We have to come back again later.  </p>
<p begin="01:17:20.880" end="01:17:24.400" style="s2">My skin&#39;s going to roast. House Valiant <br />reported on their own. Didn&#39;t even need  </p>
<p begin="01:17:24.400" end="01:17:32.560" style="s2">an escort. Some people dragged it out for <br />3 days and still had to be marched here.</p>
<p begin="01:17:32.560" end="01:17:35.760" style="s2">Well, you made it.</p>
<p begin="01:17:37.760" end="01:17:45.280" style="s2">Nina, don&#39;t get smug. I</p>
<p begin="01:17:45.280" end="01:17:51.280" style="s2">better be good. This is Ember Rift. Aren&#39;t you <br />afraid you&#39;ll disturb the sea of fire? I don&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="01:17:51.280" end="01:17:56.560" style="s2">believe you dare. You insane girl. This is Ember <br />Rift. If that thing detonates and stirs the fire,  </p>
<p begin="01:17:56.560" end="01:18:01.040" style="s2">you&#39;ll be the first one dead. Telepathy. My <br />fathers can do that, too. I knew the old man  </p>
<p begin="01:18:01.040" end="01:18:06.000" style="s2">from the archive was powerful. Oh, it&#39;s you. <br />Finished the dream fruit wine already. I have  </p>
<p begin="01:18:06.000" end="01:18:11.040" style="s2">more. Want some? Don&#39;t change the subject. You <br />do not set those things off at Ember Rift. You  </p>
<p begin="01:18:11.040" end="01:18:15.360" style="s2">couldn&#39;t bear the consequences. But sir, she <br />keeps threatening me. When she threatens me,  </p>
<p begin="01:18:15.360" end="01:18:19.440" style="s2">I just can&#39;t help myself. What am I supposed <br />to do? Veil girl, provoke another fight and  </p>
<p begin="01:18:19.440" end="01:18:25.840" style="s2">you&#39;ll stay an extra month. And you set off one <br />more explosion here and I&#39;ll throw you into the  </p>
<p begin="01:18:25.840" end="01:18:33.040" style="s2">sea of fire so you can explode to your heart&#39;s <br />content. Did he just steal my thunderburst orb?</p>
<p begin="01:18:37.600" end="01:18:46.160" style="s2">Saurin, you finally came. You&#39;ve suffered, Livia. <br />I brought you Virgin SAB. It treats fireburns.  </p>
<p begin="01:18:46.160" end="01:18:49.920" style="s2">This should make you more comfortable. Thank <br />you. You don&#39;t need to thank me. I should have  </p>
<p begin="01:18:49.920" end="01:18:55.040" style="s2">brought it sooner. You&#39;ve suffered so much. <br />If this place is hard on blade mages like us,  </p>
<p begin="01:18:55.040" end="01:19:02.000" style="s2">that light magic Nina must be burning alive <br />by now. Well, look at you two rehearsing a  </p>
<p begin="01:19:02.000" end="01:19:10.800" style="s2">romance. Your face. How is it completely fine? <br />None of your business. You&#39;re a light agent.  </p>
<p begin="01:19:10.800" end="01:19:14.640" style="s2">There&#39;s no way the fire didn&#39;t burn you. You <br />must have slipped away. Fleeing a sentence is  </p>
<p begin="01:19:14.640" end="01:19:20.960" style="s2">a serious offense. I&#39;m reporting you to <br />the chancellor and having you expelled.</p>
<p begin="01:19:20.960" end="01:19:25.600" style="s2">Did the heat cook your brain? The arch master <br />is guarding this place. How could I leave?  </p>
<p begin="01:19:25.600" end="01:19:32.480" style="s2">Unless you&#39;re accusing him of covering for me. <br />I nearly blew the cauldron. All three of you,  </p>
<p begin="01:19:32.480" end="01:19:50.480" style="s2">your sentences are extended to three months. What? <br />3 months? This is all those two Jinx&#39;s fault.</p>
<p begin="01:19:50.480" end="01:19:54.080" style="s2">Frost fruit. You can count the mages in all Cloudr  </p>
<p begin="01:19:54.080" end="01:20:03.920" style="s2">Rent who possess Frost Fruit on <br />one hand. Where did you get those?</p>
<p begin="01:20:03.920" end="01:20:10.480" style="s2">So refreshing. Food, drink, nice view. <br />Three months will fly by. Nina, don&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="01:20:10.480" end="01:20:18.000" style="s2">fall for it. Saurin, she&#39;s trying to provoke <br />you so the arch master will punish us again.</p>
<p begin="01:20:25.080" end="01:20:26.080" style="s2">[sighs]</p>
<p begin="01:20:26.080" end="01:20:31.440" style="s2">The girl awakened flame activity too.</p>
<p begin="01:20:31.440" end="01:20:36.480" style="s2">Girl, my elixir is finished, so I&#39;m <br />heading back. Lucky you. Your flame  </p>
<p begin="01:20:36.480" end="01:20:42.880" style="s2">of fatid awakened. Light is gentle enough <br />to balance flame&#39;s violence. Train well,  </p>
<p begin="01:20:42.880" end="01:20:51.280" style="s2">and your future is limitless. But light <br />and flame aren&#39;t my only affinities.</p>
<p begin="01:20:51.280" end="01:20:56.400" style="s2">The six arcane efficients counterbalance <br />one another. Whenever I strengthen one,  </p>
<p begin="01:20:56.400" end="01:21:00.880" style="s2">I have to recalibrate the other five <br />or my mana channels could ruptures  </p>
<p begin="01:21:00.880" end="01:21:06.400" style="s2">when I advance. Maintaining all six <br />is why I&#39;m still only third rank.  </p>
<p begin="01:21:06.400" end="01:21:14.960" style="s2">Even an arch from the archive doesn&#39;t <br />understand what that takes. [snorts]</p>
<p begin="01:21:14.960" end="01:21:21.200" style="s2">Where is that smell of blood coming from?</p>
<p begin="01:21:21.200" end="01:21:33.840" style="s2">Why is cold air coming from that cave?</p>
<p begin="01:21:33.840" end="01:21:40.320" style="s2">Who is he?</p>
<p begin="01:21:40.320" end="01:21:48.080" style="s2">[sighs and gasps]  </p>
<p begin="01:21:48.080" end="01:21:55.520" style="s2">He&#39;s gorgeous. Are you a student <br />of Astall Academy? Don&#39;t be afraid.  </p>
<p begin="01:21:55.520" end="01:22:08.960" style="s2">I&#39;ve been imprisoned here for 10 years. <br />My magic is sealed. I can&#39;t hurt you.</p>
<p begin="01:22:08.960" end="01:22:16.960" style="s2">Who are you? Why are you imprisoned here? Who <br />I am doesn&#39;t matter. What matters is Astal  </p>
<p begin="01:22:16.960" end="01:22:25.200" style="s2">imprisons people without ever asking why. <br />10 years ago, I accidentally broke one of  </p>
<p begin="01:22:25.200" end="01:22:33.840" style="s2">the academyy&#39;s enchanted relics. They chained <br />me here and buried me in darkness. 10 years  </p>
<p begin="01:22:33.840" end="01:22:39.200" style="s2">without sunlight or another human voice. <br />I don&#39;t even know if my parents are alive.  </p>
<p begin="01:22:39.840" end="01:22:46.080" style="s2">They chained you up for 10 years over one <br />broken relic. You&#39;re an Astall student.  </p>
<p begin="01:22:46.080" end="01:22:58.240" style="s2">You know better than I how harsh its rules <br />can be. Leave, girl. You shouldn&#39;t be here.</p>
<p begin="01:22:58.240" end="01:23:02.320" style="s2">This way. After all these years, <br />I&#39;ve stopped dreaming of escape.  </p>
<p begin="01:23:02.960" end="01:23:13.360" style="s2">Sometimes I still think if I could see <br />sunlight once more, I could die content.</p>
<p begin="01:23:13.360" end="01:23:21.840" style="s2">How can I help you? All you have to do is <br />channel magic into that signal plate. The  </p>
<p begin="01:23:21.840" end="01:23:29.840" style="s2">seal will loosen. Once I&#39;m free, I&#39;ll repay <br />you tenfold. Foolish girl. Once I break  </p>
<p begin="01:23:29.840" end="01:23:44.320" style="s2">free and claim the violet thunder flame, <br />I&#39;ll rave a fall academy to the ground.</p>
<p begin="01:23:44.320" end="01:23:56.240" style="s2">Stop.</p>
<p begin="01:23:56.240" end="01:24:02.800" style="s2">Nina, what are you doing? I should ask you that. <br />How dare you break the seal on someone imprisoned  </p>
<p begin="01:24:02.800" end="01:24:10.960" style="s2">in an academy forbidden zone? Are you insane? He&#39;s <br />not evil. He broke one enchanted relic and they  </p>
<p begin="01:24:10.960" end="01:24:20.480" style="s2">imprisoned him for 10 years. How is that fair? <br />You actually believe that garbage? Clever. One  </p>
<p begin="01:24:20.480" end="01:24:26.880" style="s2">look and you knew I was lying. Too bad you&#39;re <br />late. The little kitten already broke my seal.</p>
<p begin="01:24:38.400" end="01:24:43.040" style="s2">Arch Mayare</p>
<p begin="01:24:43.040" end="01:24:54.320" style="s2">Nyxar, your seal is broken. Old <br />man, I don&#39;t have time to reminisce.</p>
<p begin="01:24:54.320" end="01:24:56.000" style="s2">You won&#39;t escape.</p>
<p begin="01:25:00.800" end="01:25:12.400" style="s2">Good thing I sensed something was <br />wrong and warned the arch magister.</p>
<p begin="01:25:12.400" end="01:25:22.560" style="s2">The sea of fire is erupting.</p>
<p begin="01:25:22.560" end="01:25:27.440" style="s2">Good quality. Noxar wants the violet thunder flame  </p>
<p begin="01:25:27.440" end="01:25:39.440" style="s2">deep in the fire sea. He&#39;s deliberately <br />luring the archmaster to the crater.</p>
<p begin="01:25:47.360" end="01:25:54.880" style="s2">He&#39;s coming right at us.</p>
<p begin="01:25:54.880" end="01:26:06.960" style="s2">Brat, you nearly ruined my plan. I&#39;ll use this <br />violet thunderflame to send you to your grave.</p>
<p begin="01:26:12.000" end="01:26:22.240" style="s2">Nina, run. You think a little lightning fire <br />can hurt me? A mere insect dares to defy.</p>
<p begin="01:26:22.240" end="01:26:27.040" style="s2">Impossible. I haven&#39;t even refined the violet <br />thunderflame. How could that worthless pot swallow  </p>
<p begin="01:26:27.040" end="01:26:36.400" style="s2">it? Maxar, you&#39;re not getting away. Give me <br />back my flame, idiot. You&#39;ll pay for this, brat.</p>
<p begin="01:26:39.040" end="01:26:43.680" style="s2">Nina, what kind of enchanted relic is that? <br />It absorbed the violet thunder flame. It&#39;s a  </p>
<p begin="01:26:43.680" end="01:26:49.440" style="s2">divine artifact. A ridiculously powerful one. <br />You&#39;re lying. Divine artifacts vanished ages  </p>
<p begin="01:26:49.440" end="01:26:58.480" style="s2">ago. Then call it a really good cast iron <br />pot. As long as it absorbs fire, who cares?</p>
<p begin="01:26:58.480" end="01:27:04.160" style="s2">Arch mass, did you catch Nyxar?</p>
<p begin="01:27:04.160" end="01:27:09.760" style="s2">He got away. He was already wounded and <br />the violet thunder flame turned on him.  </p>
<p begin="01:27:09.760" end="01:27:13.760" style="s2">He won&#39;t cause trouble again anytime soon. <br />Then why didn&#39;t you kill him while you had  </p>
<p begin="01:27:13.760" end="01:27:19.760" style="s2">the chance? You think I didn&#39;t want to? The fire <br />sea is unstable. If I&#39;d pressed the fight here,  </p>
<p begin="01:27:19.760" end="01:27:24.960" style="s2">the whole Ember Rift could have collapsed and <br />taken the academy with it. Outside the rift,  </p>
<p begin="01:27:24.960" end="01:27:30.240" style="s2">I would have ended him with one strike. <br />Enough. We&#39;ll hunt him later. Give me  </p>
<p begin="01:27:30.240" end="01:27:36.720" style="s2">your pot. Arch Mister, I cook with this. It&#39;s <br />been with me for years. I saw that pot swallow  </p>
<p begin="01:27:36.720" end="01:27:43.280" style="s2">Afall&#39;s violet thunder flame. I I didn&#39;t tell <br />it to. It swallowed the flame by itself. Take  </p>
<p begin="01:27:43.280" end="01:27:52.800" style="s2">it out if you can. I certainly can&#39;t. Once this <br />pot swallows something, it never gives it back.</p>
<p begin="01:27:52.800" end="01:28:00.560" style="s2">This is absurd. Who is that girl? Why is <br />everything she owns an enchanted relic?</p>
<p begin="01:28:00.560" end="01:28:08.480" style="s2">[sighs and gasps] Is this the entrance to <br />Ember Rift? The Archmiss must have sent us  </p>
<p begin="01:28:08.480" end="01:28:14.480" style="s2">out so we wouldn&#39;t get hurt inside. Nina, <br />let&#39;s return to House Valiant. You exposed  </p>
<p begin="01:28:14.480" end="01:28:19.920" style="s2">a dangerous enemy inside the academy. I expect <br />they&#39;ll wave the month and a half left on your  </p>
<p begin="01:28:19.920" end="01:28:27.280" style="s2">sentence. This trip to Ember Rift may have <br />worked in your favor after all. Owen Cross  </p>
<p begin="01:28:27.280" end="01:28:40.320" style="s2">of the Chancellor&#39;s Tower. By Chancellor <br />Shaw&#39;s order, I have come for Nina Rowan.</p>
<p begin="01:28:40.320" end="01:28:48.080" style="s2">Leon, Nenina, are all the Chancellor students this <br />formal? The Chancellor trained him personally.  </p>
<p begin="01:28:48.080" end="01:28:52.640" style="s2">Owen is famous for following every rules to the <br />letter. Watch what you say. Good to meet you,  </p>
<p begin="01:28:52.640" end="01:28:58.160" style="s2">Ovin. Chancellor Shaw has learned that you <br />discovered Nyxar and warned the academy.  </p>
<p begin="01:28:58.160" end="01:29:06.400" style="s2">By his order, your remaining sentence at Ember <br />Ridge is wedded. Did they catch Nikar? Not yet.  </p>
<p begin="01:29:06.400" end="01:29:12.000" style="s2">Senior faculty are pursuing him. We should have <br />news within a few days. In a story like this,  </p>
<p begin="01:29:12.000" end="01:29:17.040" style="s2">saying that guarantees they won&#39;t catch him. <br />What about Livia? A fireball didn&#39;t kill her,  </p>
<p begin="01:29:17.040" end="01:29:22.400" style="s2">did it? Livia and Saurin were struck by <br />falling fireballs. They&#39;re still unconscious.  </p>
<p begin="01:29:22.400" end="01:29:29.520" style="s2">When Livery awakes, she&#39;ll have to answer to the <br />discipline hall. Then I&#39;ll take my leave. Wait,  </p>
<p begin="01:29:29.520" end="01:29:37.120" style="s2">what about my pot? When do I get it back? [clears <br />throat] The Chancellor still has it. If you&#39;re  </p>
<p begin="01:29:37.120" end="01:29:42.560" style="s2">worried, come with me to the Chancellor&#39;s <br />tower and ask him yourself. Arch Mage,  </p>
<p begin="01:29:42.560" end="01:29:48.000" style="s2">have you learned anything from the material? <br />It isn&#39;t star iron or arctic gold. I&#39;ve never  </p>
<p begin="01:29:48.000" end="01:29:52.880" style="s2">seen craftsmanship like this either. No one <br />in Cloudright could make it. Can you extract  </p>
<p begin="01:29:52.880" end="01:30:00.320" style="s2">the violet thunder flame? The girl said it <br />couldn&#39;t be removed. I didn&#39;t believe her,  </p>
<p begin="01:30:00.320" end="01:30:08.640" style="s2">but she was telling the truth. Then the pot <br />goes back to the girl, of course. Keep it any  </p>
<p begin="01:30:08.640" end="01:30:14.640" style="s2">longer and she&#39;ll accuse a room full of old <br />men of shamelessly stealing from her. But the  </p>
<p begin="01:30:14.640" end="01:30:20.640" style="s2">violet thunder flame. Can you extract it? We <br />may not have recovered the flame, but at least  </p>
<p begin="01:30:20.640" end="01:30:26.320" style="s2">it hasn&#39;t left Astall. It&#39;s in the hands of one <br />of our own students. Leave it there. Archmaster,  </p>
<p begin="01:30:26.320" end="01:30:30.000" style="s2">you planned to give her the rare flame from the <br />start, didn&#39;t you? These past two days of research  </p>
<p begin="01:30:30.000" end="01:30:41.360" style="s2">were just for appearances. I was going to give <br />it to her. You have a problem with that? [sighs]</p>
<p begin="01:30:41.360" end="01:30:45.120" style="s2">Can I have my pot back now?</p>
<p begin="01:30:47.600" end="01:30:55.120" style="s2">So, this is the pot that swallowed <br />the violet thunder flame.</p>
<p begin="01:30:55.120" end="01:31:00.560" style="s2">Nixxar failed this time, but he&#39;ll <br />come back. Most people at Astl think  </p>
<p begin="01:31:00.560" end="01:31:06.400" style="s2">the rare flame is still inside him. That <br />protects you. Unless the truth gets out,  </p>
<p begin="01:31:06.400" end="01:31:12.960" style="s2">then everyone will come after you. Honestly, you <br />shouldn&#39;t have told even us. I don&#39;t care. This  </p>
<p begin="01:31:12.960" end="01:31:20.480" style="s2">pot keeps me fed. Anyone who tries to take it <br />dies. Libby broke the seal and released Nixxar,  </p>
<p begin="01:31:20.480" end="01:31:25.200" style="s2">so they added three months to her sentence. Saurin <br />attacked a discipline prefate for her and earned  </p>
<p begin="01:31:25.200" end="01:31:36.080" style="s2">three more months, too. [snorts] Saurin is the <br />loyal second lead in every romance. Loyal. Don&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="01:31:36.080" end="01:31:45.120" style="s2">you see it? He&#39;s like a faithful dog, always <br />circling Livia. Now that you mention it, he is</p>
<p begin="01:31:45.120" end="01:31:58.240" style="s2">Enough gossip. I&#39;m going to the Grand Archive <br />for a new Grammanoy. Stop right there.</p>
<p begin="01:31:58.240" end="01:32:04.880" style="s2">You&#39;re Nina Rowan, House <br />Valiant&#39;s new ETH student.</p>
<p begin="01:32:04.880" end="01:32:12.080" style="s2">That&#39;s me. What do you want? Nina Rowan. Our <br />youngest protege suffered in Ember Rift because  </p>
<p begin="01:32:12.080" end="01:32:17.440" style="s2">of you. Did you think we&#39;d let that go? If you <br />can&#39;t let it go, join her at Ember Rift. You can  </p>
<p begin="01:32:17.440" end="01:32:26.320" style="s2">make a full table. Why bother me? Don&#39;t get cocky, <br />Nina. Do you really think no one dares touch you?  </p>
<p begin="01:32:26.320" end="01:32:32.480" style="s2">If you&#39;re going to fight, hurry up. Otherwise, <br />move. It&#39;s always the same tired lines. If you&#39;re  </p>
<p begin="01:32:32.480" end="01:32:38.720" style="s2">not bored saying them, I&#39;m bored hearing them. You <br />You&#39;ve got some nerve. I do. If you don&#39;t like it,  </p>
<p begin="01:32:38.720" end="01:32:43.920" style="s2">kill me. Nina, take down the witness mirrors at <br />the League Arena. Otherwise, you won&#39;t be able  </p>
<p begin="01:32:43.920" end="01:32:49.680" style="s2">to handle the consequences. And lose face because <br />you ordered me to. No chance. Let&#39;s see how long  </p>
<p begin="01:32:49.680" end="01:32:58.320" style="s2">that arrogance lasts. If you won&#39;t listen to <br />reason, just wait. Come on, we&#39;re leaving.</p>
<p begin="01:32:58.320" end="01:33:02.000" style="s2">Are they insane? They blocked <br />my path just to threaten me. I  </p>
<p begin="01:33:02.000" end="01:33:05.840" style="s2">stay quiet once and suddenly <br />they think I&#39;m Hello Chitty.</p>
<p begin="01:33:07.920" end="01:33:14.000" style="s2">What happened? Is the fire sea erupting <br />again? 50 mid-grade Ava crystals. Perks,  </p>
<p begin="01:33:14.000" end="01:33:19.600" style="s2">I need you to investigate something.</p>
<p begin="01:33:19.600" end="01:33:27.280" style="s2">We&#39;re family. Of course you came to me. What do <br />you want to know? Find out how Livia met those  </p>
<p begin="01:33:27.280" end="01:33:34.240" style="s2">storm glass prodigies and her mentor and how <br />they treat one another. I want every detail.</p>
<p begin="01:33:40.640" end="01:33:47.280" style="s2">I found it. What you asked me to investigate <br />is fascinating. No wonder Luke had dots on his  </p>
<p begin="01:33:47.280" end="01:33:52.160" style="s2">youngest student. It turns out they knew each <br />other before she ever enrolled. Oh. A few years  </p>
<p begin="01:33:52.160" end="01:33:56.240" style="s2">ago, Luke had found Livia under attack in the <br />Cloudwilled Mountains and rushed in to save her.  </p>
<p begin="01:33:56.240" end="01:33:59.680" style="s2">He admitted her as his personal prodigy before the <br />enrollment trials even began. Admission without  </p>
<p begin="01:33:59.680" end="01:34:05.680" style="s2">an exam. That&#39;s one enormous favor. There&#39;s more. <br />Reportedly, Livia spent several nights in Lucan&#39;s  </p>
<p begin="01:34:05.680" end="01:34:11.600" style="s2">quarters. Pierce, don&#39;t repeat a claim like that <br />without proof. Lucan is known throughout Aston  </p>
<p begin="01:34:11.600" end="01:34:16.160" style="s2">for keeping everyone at a distance. To say he <br />kept a female student in his quarters overnight,  </p>
<p begin="01:34:16.160" end="01:34:20.880" style="s2">I&#39;m not making it up, Leon. Livia keeps <br />spare clothes in Lucan&#39;s quarters. And  </p>
<p begin="01:34:20.880" end="01:34:26.240" style="s2">that&#39;s not all. Since the day she enrolled, <br />her fellow proteges have acted enchanted. They  </p>
<p begin="01:34:26.240" end="01:34:31.200" style="s2">obey her every word and treat her orders like <br />favors. Who wouldn&#39;t call that a charmed life?  </p>
<p begin="01:34:31.200" end="01:34:36.480" style="s2">A heroic rescue, a mentor sent from heaven. <br />Everyone adors her and she can do no wrong.  </p>
<p begin="01:34:36.480" end="01:34:40.480" style="s2">She&#39;s the pampered heroine in her own <br />romance. Nina, what are you planning to  </p>
<p begin="01:34:40.480" end="01:34:46.720" style="s2">do with all this? Write a story. Don&#39;t you <br />think this is incredibly dramatic? Storm  </p>
<p begin="01:34:46.720" end="01:34:51.840" style="s2">Glass keeps cornering me with threats. Do they <br />think healers don&#39;t count? They love treating  </p>
<p begin="01:34:51.840" end="01:34:59.440" style="s2">her like their precious darling. Fine, I&#39;ll show <br />the entire academy exactly how they spoil her.</p>
<p begin="01:35:02.000" end="01:35:06.240" style="s2">Nina, Lucan has returned from private <br />training. He also pulled Livia and Sarin  </p>
<p begin="01:35:06.240" end="01:35:10.560" style="s2">out of Ember Rift. So that&#39;s what <br />those two geniuses meant by just  </p>
<p begin="01:35:10.560" end="01:35:15.040" style="s2">wait. There&#39;s more. Lucan knocked down <br />all 10 witness mirrors you placed at  </p>
<p begin="01:35:15.040" end="01:35:28.800" style="s2">the League Arena. What? He thinks he can <br />steal my witness mirrors. Not a chance.</p>
<p begin="01:35:28.800" end="01:35:32.320" style="s2">Chancellor, someone stole my <br />property. Are you going to  </p>
<p begin="01:35:32.320" end="01:35:42.720" style="s2">do something about it? Who? Lucan <br />Storm, head of House Storm Glass.</p>
<p begin="01:35:42.720" end="01:35:47.760" style="s2">That face is impressive. No wonder Leon said <br />he&#39;s impossible to approach. Too bad his taste  </p>
<p begin="01:35:47.760" end="01:35:52.960" style="s2">is awful. He fell for a fake innocent. Why did <br />you summon me, Chancellor Lucan? You came out of  </p>
<p begin="01:35:52.960" end="01:35:56.720" style="s2">private training and immediately took down all <br />10 of my witness mirrors. Those are my private  </p>
<p begin="01:35:56.720" end="01:36:00.320" style="s2">relics. You can&#39;t just seize them. That&#39;s theft. <br />You were broadcast images that damaged house  </p>
<p begin="01:36:00.320" end="01:36:04.800" style="s2">storm glass reputation and invited ridicule of my <br />students. I removed the mirrors to preserve order  </p>
<p begin="01:36:04.800" end="01:36:09.520" style="s2">at the academy. Preserve order. Every image was <br />real. If you&#39;re worried about damaged reputations,  </p>
<p begin="01:36:09.520" end="01:36:15.040" style="s2">take it up with your students father. Lyra put you <br />up to this, didn&#39;t she? Go tell her she wanted to  </p>
<p begin="01:36:15.040" end="01:36:19.600" style="s2">anger me and she succeeded. But she should never <br />have dragged Livia into it. I&#39;ll go to House  </p>
<p begin="01:36:19.600" end="01:36:23.760" style="s2">Valiant myself and demand an answer. Of course, <br />all the idiots found one another. His own student  </p>
<p begin="01:36:23.760" end="01:36:28.320" style="s2">caused this mess and somehow he blames my mentor. <br />Chancellor, listen. He&#39;ll say anything except I&#39;ll  </p>
<p begin="01:36:28.320" end="01:36:33.600" style="s2">pay. Academy Code section 256621. Any student, <br />dean, or head of her house who refuses serious  </p>
<p begin="01:36:33.600" end="01:36:37.920" style="s2">matter may be stripped of office and at Enkfeld. <br />Does this girl eat the academy code for breakfast?  </p>
<p begin="01:36:37.920" end="01:36:43.840" style="s2">How did she remember all of it? Very well. A mere <br />third rank student thinks she can expel me from  </p>
<p begin="01:36:43.840" end="01:36:49.840" style="s2">the academy. Chancellor, look, he&#39;s panicking. <br />He wants to silence me. Please stop talking.  </p>
<p begin="01:36:49.840" end="01:36:55.760" style="s2">Keep this up and even I&#39;ll want to silence <br />you. Lucin Nina may have been disrespectful,  </p>
<p begin="01:36:55.760" end="01:37:00.240" style="s2">but discipline belongs to House Valiant. <br />Attacking her would be improper. Exactly.  </p>
<p begin="01:37:00.240" end="01:37:04.560" style="s2">If Storm Blast wants my witness mirrors, just say <br />so. I have plenty. Maybe I&#39;ll donate a few. But  </p>
<p begin="01:37:04.560" end="01:37:16.720" style="s2">taking them without permission is stealing. Is <br />petty theft really fitting for a head of house?</p>
<p begin="01:37:16.720" end="01:37:23.600" style="s2">Daddy.</p>
<p begin="01:37:23.600" end="01:37:30.320" style="s2">Lyra. Lucan Storm. Picking on my student <br />while I&#39;m gone. You must be itching for  </p>
