<p begin="01:56:22.960" end="01:56:27.840" style="s2">Sorry. Then I won&#39;t use it. No sword, no <br />branch. You mean to fight me bare-handed,  </p>
<p begin="01:56:27.840" end="01:56:33.760" style="s2">Leon? That&#39;s even more insulting.</p>
<p begin="01:56:33.760" end="01:56:43.680" style="s2">Is this better?</p>
<p begin="01:56:57.760" end="01:57:04.240" style="s2">House Valiian Leon Arden wins. Was that <br />really a branch? Just a dead branch? I  </p>
<p begin="01:57:04.240" end="01:57:07.280" style="s2">heard Leon has never drawn his sword since <br />coming to the academy. I thought he couldn&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="01:57:07.280" end="01:57:11.360" style="s2">use one. Turns out he simply doesn&#39;t need <br />one. So, this is Leon&#39;s true strength. He  </p>
<p begin="01:57:11.360" end="01:57:18.240" style="s2">dismantled a fourth ranked blade mash <br />with a dead branch. That&#39;s incredible.</p>
<p begin="01:57:18.240" end="01:57:24.240" style="s2">House Valance as Bellamy wins.</p>
<p begin="01:57:24.240" end="01:57:29.120" style="s2">I surrender. House Valiants Quinn <br />Mailor wins. He laid wards so fast  </p>
<p begin="01:57:29.120" end="01:57:36.320" style="s2">that his opponent got trapped and <br />surrendered. Quinn is ridiculous.</p>
<p begin="01:57:36.320" end="01:57:44.320" style="s2">Weak. House Valiant. Julian Frost win. House <br />Valiant. Ian Blake wins. What just happened?  </p>
<p begin="01:57:44.320" end="01:57:49.120" style="s2">Who was fighting? I can&#39;t remember any of it. I <br />missed it, too. But House Valant is incredible.  </p>
<p begin="01:57:49.120" end="01:58:00.400" style="s2">At this rate, first place is theirs. Livia Bal <br />of House Storm Glass requests priority selection.</p>
<p begin="01:58:00.400" end="01:58:06.800" style="s2">I challenge Nina Rowan of House Valiant.</p>
<p begin="01:58:06.800" end="01:58:10.880" style="s2">Nina? Isn&#39;t she a light mage? A blade <br />mage against a light mage. This should  </p>
<p begin="01:58:10.880" end="01:58:16.240" style="s2">be effortless. Those two have a blood feed. <br />With the new rules banning Thunderbird orbs,  </p>
<p begin="01:58:16.240" end="01:58:21.280" style="s2">Livia must be planning to take <br />revenge in front of everyone.</p>
<p begin="01:58:21.280" end="01:58:26.480" style="s2">Livia, she&#39;s only a light magent. Let me <br />fight her for you. Exactly. You rest. Leave  </p>
<p begin="01:58:26.480" end="01:58:32.800" style="s2">her to us. Thank you, both of you. But this is <br />between Nina and me. I want to settle it myself.  </p>
<p begin="01:58:33.760" end="01:58:41.440" style="s2">Nina Rowan, without Thunderb or orbs, what will <br />you use to stop my sword? Nina, your Thunderbird  </p>
<p begin="01:58:41.440" end="01:58:47.840" style="s2">orbs are banned. Are you sure you&#39;ll be okay? <br />Of course she won&#39;t. She&#39;s a light mage with  </p>
<p begin="01:58:47.840" end="01:58:52.880" style="s2">no combat ability. She should surrender before <br />she embarrasses House Valiant. Julian, if you  </p>
<p begin="01:58:52.880" end="01:59:00.640" style="s2">can&#39;t say anything useful, say nothing. Relax. <br />If things get bad, I still have healing magic.</p>
<p begin="01:59:03.360" end="01:59:13.760" style="s2">Your healing magic does qualify as an attack. Just <br />don&#39;t use it on yourself. Right. Definitely don&#39;t.</p>
<p begin="01:59:13.760" end="01:59:19.600" style="s2">Both fighters take the platform.</p>
<p begin="01:59:19.600" end="01:59:28.320" style="s2">I&#39;m up. Good luck, Nina. <br />Don&#39;t embarrass House Valish.</p>
<p begin="01:59:28.320" end="01:59:33.280" style="s2">Nina, you can still surrender. Kneel and <br />apologize in front of everyone and I may  </p>
<p begin="01:59:33.280" end="01:59:56.640" style="s2">spare you. Can we start? I still have <br />a gale hair waiting back at the house.</p>
<p begin="01:59:56.640" end="02:00:00.160" style="s2">That sword&#39;s error is even stronger than <br />frost blues. It has to be a legendary  </p>
<p begin="02:00:00.160" end="02:00:03.120" style="s2">grade artifact. Lucan must have given <br />it to her. She loses one sword and gets  </p>
<p begin="02:00:03.120" end="02:00:06.400" style="s2">an even better one. Livia really is <br />blessed. Nah&#39;s thunderburst orbs are  </p>
<p begin="02:00:06.400" end="02:00:09.840" style="s2">banned and Livia has a new bonded blade. <br />This match is already over. Don&#39;t worry,  </p>
<p begin="02:00:09.840" end="02:00:20.320" style="s2">Nina. I won&#39;t kill you in one strike. I&#39;ll cut you <br />down piece by piece until you understand despair.</p>
<p begin="02:00:20.320" end="02:00:23.440" style="s2">What kind of footwork is that? Livia has <br />struck dozens of times and hasn&#39;t landed  </p>
<p begin="02:00:23.440" end="02:00:27.040" style="s2">once. Isn&#39;t Nina a light mage? She slips <br />away like an eel. She must have trained  </p>
<p begin="02:00:27.040" end="02:00:34.160" style="s2">nothing but dodging cuz she can&#39;t fight. <br />If you can&#39;t win, run. Smart enough.</p>
<p begin="02:00:34.160" end="02:00:39.440" style="s2">That&#39;s Nina for you. [sighs and gasps] Aren&#39;t <br />you a blade major? How are you running out of  </p>
<p begin="02:00:39.440" end="02:00:56.240" style="s2">breath before a light aegist? Need <br />a break? I can wait. Heaven first.</p>
<p begin="02:01:08.480" end="02:01:14.800" style="s2">fire. How could she use fire? Isn&#39;t she a light <br />mage? A spell glyph? It has to be a flame glyph.  </p>
<p begin="02:01:14.800" end="02:01:19.440" style="s2">The first new rule bans single-use combat <br />glyphs. She cheated. So that&#39;s why she kept  </p>
<p begin="02:01:19.440" end="02:01:25.440" style="s2">dodging. She was waiting to ambush Livia <br />with a glyph. Nina is a flame mate, too.  </p>
<p begin="02:01:26.080" end="02:01:30.720" style="s2">Better than being limited to light, I suppose.</p>
<p begin="02:01:30.720" end="02:01:36.160" style="s2">Interesting. Nina Rowan, the chancellor explicitly <br />banned single-use glyphs. You cheated in front of  </p>
<p begin="02:01:36.160" end="02:01:41.680" style="s2">everyone. You should lose immediately. Who said <br />this came from a gaff? I use light and flame.  </p>
<p begin="02:01:41.680" end="02:01:48.160" style="s2">Never seen a dual affinity mation. Impossible. <br />You&#39;re a light mation. Then I guess you haven&#39;t.  </p>
<p begin="02:01:48.160" end="02:01:57.920" style="s2">You used your finishing move. Now it&#39;s my <br />turn. By flame and fury, none stat above me.</p>
<p begin="02:01:57.920" end="02:02:04.600" style="s2">House Valiance Nina Rowan wins.</p>
<p begin="02:02:04.600" end="02:02:14.400" style="s2">[laughter] Saurin, she humiliated me in <br />front of everyone. [gasps] Don&#39;t worry,  </p>
<p begin="02:02:14.400" end="02:02:19.920" style="s2">Livia. I&#39;ll avenge you.</p>
<p begin="02:02:21.440" end="02:02:27.440" style="s2">Saurin Hail of House Storm Glass invokes <br />priority selection. I challenge Nina Rowan  </p>
<p begin="02:02:27.440" end="02:02:31.040" style="s2">of House Valance. Saurin is late fifth <br />rank and he&#39;s challenging a third rank  </p>
<p begin="02:02:31.040" end="02:02:34.880" style="s2">major. That&#39;s bullying. Didn&#39;t you read the <br />Beast King&#39;s Bride? The male leader throws his  </p>
<p begin="02:02:34.880" end="02:02:38.800" style="s2">life away every time his beloved junior cries. <br />Think Saurin is the real life version. Sora,  </p>
<p begin="02:02:38.800" end="02:02:42.880" style="s2">you&#39;re fifth rank, she&#39;s third rank, and you&#39;re <br />forcing her into back-to-back matches. Have you  </p>
<p begin="02:02:42.880" end="02:02:48.160" style="s2">no shame? Exactly. Nina just finished a <br />match. This isn&#39;t fair. If you&#39;re afraid,  </p>
<p begin="02:02:48.160" end="02:02:57.280" style="s2">surrender. But for fitting without a <br />fight costs 50 points. Fine, I accept.</p>
<p begin="02:02:57.280" end="02:03:06.800" style="s2">Don&#39;t worry. Beating Livia barely <br />cost me any manner. Call it a warm-up.</p>
<p begin="02:03:06.800" end="02:03:11.120" style="s2">She called beating Livia a warm-up. That <br />That&#39;s arrogant. Sergeant is fiercely  </p>
<p begin="02:03:11.120" end="02:03:15.600" style="s2">protective. After that insult, Nina is in for <br />a brutal lesson. Even with light and flame,  </p>
<p begin="02:03:15.600" end="02:03:21.520" style="s2">third rank against fifth rank is an enormous gap. <br />House Valiant may be about to lose its lead. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="02:03:21.520" end="02:03:34.320" style="s2">are you sure you have enough <br />mana left? Don&#39;t worry, Leon.</p>
<p begin="02:03:34.320" end="02:03:41.120" style="s2">One fight and I&#39;m actually a little hungry. A <br />vert elixir fruit. That&#39;s a priceless healing  </p>
<p begin="02:03:41.120" end="02:03:44.800" style="s2">treasure and she&#39;s eating it like a snack. First, <br />she used Thunderbird orbs like party poppers,  </p>
<p begin="02:03:44.800" end="02:03:49.360" style="s2">and now she produces a verant lick fruit <br />without blinking. How rich is Nina? Sora,  </p>
<p begin="02:03:49.360" end="02:03:54.320" style="s2">hit her. Show her the tournament isn&#39;t a place <br />to flaunt her money. Nina certainly knows how to  </p>
<p begin="02:03:54.320" end="02:04:07.200" style="s2">get under people&#39;s skin. Keep pretending. <br />You&#39;ll be begging for mercy soon enough.</p>
<p begin="02:04:07.200" end="02:04:12.120" style="s2">Blazing. [screaming]</p>
<p begin="02:04:28.960" end="02:04:37.520" style="s2">So much for light and flame. <br />Let&#39;s see you stop this strike.</p>
<p begin="02:04:47.920" end="02:04:51.840" style="s2">You dodged one strike. Can you <br />dodge 10? Light and flame won&#39;t  </p>
<p begin="02:04:51.840" end="02:04:54.640" style="s2">change anything. You&#39;re third rank. Eventually,  </p>
<p begin="02:04:54.640" end="02:05:05.200" style="s2">your mana will run dry. Who said I plan to <br />keep dodging? I prefer taking the initiative.</p>
<p begin="02:05:07.600" end="02:05:13.520" style="s2">Swords. She has swords, too. She&#39;s a blade <br />mage. Light, flame, and now blade magic. How  </p>
<p begin="02:05:13.520" end="02:05:17.600" style="s2">much has she been hiding? So, she is a blade <br />mage after all. So, what if you&#39;re a blade  </p>
<p begin="02:05:17.600" end="02:05:34.640" style="s2">magic? A third rank blade magic still can&#39;t <br />defeat a fifth rank one. Blazing Ark. Go.</p>
<p begin="02:05:34.640" end="02:05:42.240" style="s2">House Valiants Nina Rowan.</p>
<p begin="02:05:42.240" end="02:05:47.360" style="s2">Who said I lost?</p>
<p begin="02:05:47.360" end="02:05:51.760" style="s2">The blood burning reach. It multiplies <br />his mana 10fold for half an hour,  </p>
<p begin="02:05:51.760" end="02:05:59.840" style="s2">but afterwards he won&#39;t be able to <br />canel magic for the rest of the day.</p>
<p begin="02:05:59.840" end="02:06:03.680" style="s2">Has Solen lost his mind? It&#39;s an <br />academy tournament. Why use a right  </p>
<p begin="02:06:03.680" end="02:06:12.800" style="s2">that harms him almost as badly as his opponent?</p>
<p begin="02:06:12.800" end="02:06:18.880" style="s2">That right ravages your heart and mana <br />channels. You should never have leared it.  </p>
<p begin="02:06:18.880" end="02:06:27.680" style="s2">Spare me your fake concern. Good advice <br />can&#39;t save someone determined to die.</p>
<p begin="02:06:31.600" end="02:06:36.080" style="s2">die.</p>
<p begin="02:06:36.080" end="02:06:43.280" style="s2">No, he&#39;s aiming for a vital <br />point. He&#39;s trying to kill her.</p>
<p begin="02:06:43.280" end="02:06:51.120" style="s2">If you&#39;d knelt and surrendered, I might <br />have spared you. Now you deserve this.</p>
<p begin="02:06:51.120" end="02:06:55.120" style="s2">That&#39;s horrific. There may not be <br />anything left of her after this.  </p>
<p begin="02:06:56.080" end="02:07:02.080" style="s2">She insisted on provoking Sorish. <br />She brought this on herself.</p>
<p begin="02:07:02.080" end="02:07:08.960" style="s2">That worthless girl is finally dead.</p>
<p begin="02:07:08.960" end="02:07:24.880" style="s2">Nina will be all right, won&#39;t she? Nina has <br />plenty of relics. She&#39;ll be all right. Look.</p>
<p begin="02:07:24.880" end="02:07:35.520" style="s2">Hot, isn&#39;t it? Time for a <br />little rain to cool the arena.</p>
<p begin="02:07:35.520" end="02:07:43.040" style="s2">Water magic. She can use water, too. Light, <br />flame, water. And she&#39;s a blade mage controlling  </p>
<p begin="02:07:43.040" end="02:07:50.640" style="s2">two swords. What kind of monster is she? No, <br />that has to be a relic. Chancellor, she broke  </p>
<p begin="02:07:50.640" end="02:08:02.320" style="s2">the rules. Just how much has that girl been <br />hiding? Nina always finds a way to surprise us.</p>
<p begin="02:08:02.320" end="02:08:07.760" style="s2">No, that&#39;s impossible.</p>
<p begin="02:08:07.760" end="02:08:26.240" style="s2">This isn&#39;t over. [clears throat]</p>
<p begin="02:08:26.240" end="02:08:34.160" style="s2">referee, shouldn&#39;t you announce the <br />winner? House Valiant Nina Rowan win.</p>
<p begin="02:08:34.160" end="02:08:39.440" style="s2">A third rank mage defeated a fifth rank <br />one. I&#39;ve never heard of anything like it.  </p>
<p begin="02:08:41.040" end="02:08:44.880" style="s2">Nina, are you hurt? That fire <br />was terrifying. H You&#39;re lucky  </p>
<p begin="02:08:44.880" end="02:08:49.600" style="s2">you survived. Julian, if you don&#39;t know <br />how to praise someone, keep quiet. Nina,  </p>
<p begin="02:08:49.600" end="02:08:58.480" style="s2">take fewer fights like that. Your safety comes <br />first. Don&#39;t worry, Quinn. I know my limits.</p>
<p begin="02:08:58.480" end="02:09:05.760" style="s2">A win is a win. Ian, you <br />were here, too. Are you hurt?</p>
<p begin="02:09:06.520" end="02:09:14.320" style="s2">[gasps] Nina Rowan, just wait.</p>
<p begin="02:09:14.320" end="02:09:19.040" style="s2">Before I announce the champion, there <br />is a disciplinary ruling. Saurin Hail  </p>
<p begin="02:09:19.040" end="02:09:23.040" style="s2">is disqualified for a deliberate lethal <br />attack and will face the discipline hall  </p>
<p begin="02:09:23.040" end="02:09:30.000" style="s2">once he is medically stable. This year&#39;s Academy <br />Tournament champion with the highest score is  </p>
<p begin="02:09:30.000" end="02:09:35.200" style="s2">House Valiant. That settles it. House Valiant <br />is no longer in danger of being dissolved.</p>
<p begin="02:09:38.240" end="02:09:42.880" style="s2">Saurin&#39;s heart channels are shattered. He <br />fell from fifth rank to first. More than  </p>
<p begin="02:09:42.880" end="02:09:47.280" style="s2">half his matter channels are destroyed <br />and he&#39;s almost crippled. Chancellor,  </p>
<p begin="02:09:47.280" end="02:09:51.600" style="s2">tournament matches are supposed to stop <br />before serious harm. Nina attacked without  </p>
<p begin="02:09:51.600" end="02:09:59.680" style="s2">restraint and deliberately milled a fellow <br />student. I demand that she be punished.</p>
<p begin="02:09:59.680" end="02:10:05.200" style="s2">Without restraint. Where was this outrage when <br />Saurin used the blood burning REIT and tried to  </p>
<p begin="02:10:05.200" end="02:10:12.640" style="s2">kill Nina? He chose lethal force first. Yet you <br />blame the student who defended herself. Lucan,  </p>
<p begin="02:10:12.640" end="02:10:18.880" style="s2">even Bias should have limits. So the Chancellor <br />intends to protect Nenah. And if I do,  </p>
<p begin="02:10:18.880" end="02:10:23.280" style="s2">Nenah reached the hidden thousandth step, channels <br />light, water, and flame, and controls two swords  </p>
<p begin="02:10:23.280" end="02:10:27.120" style="s2">at once. Has this academy produced another <br />student like her in the last century? She  </p>
<p begin="02:10:27.120" end="02:10:38.640" style="s2">is the future pride of Astall. Why would I protect <br />Livia whose answer to everything is tears instead?</p>
<p begin="02:10:38.640" end="02:10:43.840" style="s2">Read it yourself. Which story in that book <br />falsely accuses your precious student,  </p>
<p begin="02:10:43.840" end="02:10:53.360" style="s2">Lucan, how long will you keep shielding her?</p>
<p begin="02:10:53.360" end="02:11:01.520" style="s2">Livia, explain this book. Mentor, Nenah <br />invented all of it to smear me. She hates me,  </p>
<p begin="02:11:01.520" end="02:11:04.640" style="s2">my father, and the entire Veil <br />family. Please don&#39;t believe  </p>
<p begin="02:11:04.640" end="02:11:13.280" style="s2">her. Is that so? Because every story <br />in here feels remarkably familiar.</p>
<p begin="02:11:13.280" end="02:11:17.760" style="s2">I used to believe whatever you told me. Even <br />when something felt wrong, I told myself not  </p>
<p begin="02:11:17.760" end="02:11:22.720" style="s2">to question you. Now I see how long I let <br />that helpless act blind me. That&#39;s not true,  </p>
<p begin="02:11:22.720" end="02:11:29.360" style="s2">mentor. It isn&#39;t. Tomorrow I will announce <br />an extended private retreat. From now on,  </p>
<p begin="02:11:29.360" end="02:11:47.840" style="s2">your affairs are no longer my concern. Mentor, <br />are you abandoning me? I know I was wrong.</p>
<p begin="02:11:47.840" end="02:11:52.800" style="s2">Men, don&#39;t blame me. All of you forced me to this.</p>
<p begin="02:11:56.160" end="02:12:02.160" style="s2">The academy has been strangely quiet. <br />The chancellor took several mentors to  </p>
<p begin="02:12:02.160" end="02:12:07.920" style="s2">the compilation of the seven arcanemies and <br />Arch Mast Olden went with them. Lucan also  </p>
<p begin="02:12:07.920" end="02:12:12.800" style="s2">announced a private retreat a few days ago. <br />Most of the academyy&#39;s strongest people are  </p>
<p begin="02:12:12.800" end="02:12:18.320" style="s2">gone. I don&#39;t like it. Quinn, when do you <br />ever feel safe? Mentor and Luca are both  </p>
<p begin="02:12:18.320" end="02:12:23.920" style="s2">away on private retreats. The chancellor, <br />Archmaster Olden, and most senior mentors  </p>
<p begin="02:12:23.920" end="02:12:37.760" style="s2">are away. Does that make House Valiant <br />the strongest force left at the academy?</p>
<p begin="02:12:37.760" end="02:12:44.080" style="s2">What is that sound?</p>
<p begin="02:12:49.520" end="02:12:58.800" style="s2">Is that a beast horde?</p>
<p begin="02:12:58.800" end="02:13:05.120" style="s2">People of Astil, listen well. You imprisoned me <br />for years. Today I collect that debt. Surrender  </p>
<p begin="02:13:05.120" end="02:13:10.320" style="s2">the violet lightning flame and Nina Rowan <br />and I may let the rest of you live. Nyxar,  </p>
<p begin="02:13:10.320" end="02:13:14.640" style="s2">you bring a beast horde against this academy <br />and think no one remains to oppose you. Enough  </p>
<p begin="02:13:14.640" end="02:13:18.480" style="s2">bluffing. Your chancellor and the other old <br />powers are hundreds of miles away. Today,  </p>
<p begin="02:13:18.480" end="02:13:24.800" style="s2">Asterfall Academy dies. All students, hear me. <br />The survival of Astrafall Academy is at stake.  </p>
<p begin="02:13:24.800" end="02:13:31.840" style="s2">We win today or we have no home left. Leon Arden <br />and Leo Ashford hold the east gate. Quinn Marcel  </p>
<p begin="02:13:31.840" end="02:13:37.440" style="s2">and Piers Bell hold the west. Julian Frost and <br />Nina Rowan take the south. Owen Cross and Livia  </p>
<p begin="02:13:37.440" end="02:13:42.960" style="s2">Vile take the north. Ian Blake, reinforcements <br />wherever the line breaks. Senior students, form  </p>
<p begin="02:13:42.960" end="02:13:47.840" style="s2">teams of five and clear any beasts that breach the <br />gates. Junior students, move supplies and treat  </p>
<p begin="02:13:47.840" end="02:14:04.880" style="s2">the wounded. Prefates, keep the ward network <br />running. Move. Hold the academy. No retreat.</p>
<p begin="02:14:04.880" end="02:14:31.040" style="s2">Leon. Stay alert. I got your back.</p>
<p begin="02:14:31.040" end="02:14:33.600" style="s2">Thank you, Quinn.</p>
<p begin="02:14:36.960" end="02:14:43.200" style="s2">Too weak. I haven&#39;t even warmed up.</p>
<p begin="02:14:43.200" end="02:14:51.120" style="s2">Julian, spend less time <br />posing and watch your back.</p>
<p begin="02:14:51.120" end="02:14:58.480" style="s2">This beast horde isn&#39;t so terrifying. Once we <br />finish this wave, I can go back to my gale hair.</p>
<p begin="02:14:58.480" end="02:15:02.800" style="s2">The north gate has fallen. Everyone fall <br />back to the central quad immediately.  </p>
<p begin="02:15:02.800" end="02:15:10.320" style="s2">Repeat, the north gate has fallen. Fall back now.</p>
<p begin="02:15:10.320" end="02:15:15.120" style="s2">Weren&#39;t Owen and Liviana defending the north <br />gate? Owen is the Chancellor&#39;s own protetéé.  </p>
<p begin="02:15:15.120" end="02:15:21.520" style="s2">How could it fall? Even if Owen couldn&#39;t stop <br />the horde, he should have been able to retreat.  </p>
<p begin="02:15:21.520" end="02:15:30.800" style="s2">Owen. Owen died protecting my retreat. The beast <br />killed him. I was useless. I couldn&#39;t save him.</p>
<p begin="02:15:36.400" end="02:15:52.782" style="s2">So much for Astall Academyy&#39;s grand ward. <br />All students, form ranks. Prepare to fight.</p>
<p begin="02:15:52.782" end="02:15:58.600" style="s2">[sighs and gasps] He&#39;s far stronger than he was at <br />Ember Rift. How did he grow this much? [laughter]  </p>
<p begin="02:16:00.080" end="02:16:04.800" style="s2">surprised. I owe my swift recovery to your cat. <br />I little kitten stole your secret medicine and  </p>
<p begin="02:16:04.800" end="02:16:09.040" style="s2">made me stronger. Then shut down the north <br />gate wards. I could hardly have asked for an  </p>
<p begin="02:16:09.040" end="02:16:17.600" style="s2">easier invasion. Livia, you brought Niter here. <br />Owen didn&#39;t die protecting you. You killed him.  </p>
<p begin="02:16:17.600" end="02:16:22.400" style="s2">So what if I did? My mentor abandoned me. <br />The chancellor punished me. And the entire  </p>
<p begin="02:16:22.400" end="02:16:29.280" style="s2">academy despises me. Astray me first. Don&#39;t <br />blame me for returning the favor. Nexar,  </p>
<p begin="02:16:29.280" end="02:16:51.600" style="s2">she&#39;s the one who ruined my life. Kill <br />her. As you command, my little kitten.</p>
<p begin="02:16:51.600" end="02:16:54.800" style="s2">A little bird dares touch my daughter.</p>
<p begin="02:17:01.680" end="02:17:08.080" style="s2">But Alden, who are you? You are not worthy of <br />knowing. Enough tricks. I&#39;ll kill you first,  </p>
<p begin="02:17:08.080" end="02:17:17.040" style="s2">then slaughter everyone in this academy.</p>
<p begin="02:17:34.399" end="02:17:43.439" style="s2">Thank you, sir. May I ask your name <br />so the academy can repay you someday?</p>
<p begin="02:17:43.439" end="02:17:50.879" style="s2">No need. I&#39;m just a lonely old father whose <br />daughter won&#39;t stay home and look after him.  </p>
<p begin="02:17:50.880" end="02:18:00.720" style="s2">You&#39;re too thin. Look how sharp your chin is, <br />Papa. Alder, my face has never been round.</p>
<p begin="02:18:00.720" end="02:18:05.760" style="s2">It was when you were five. You ate <br />three bowls of aether oats in one  </p>
<p begin="02:18:05.760" end="02:18:14.000" style="s2">sitting and your cheeks looked like <br />two dinner rolls. That was baby fat.</p>
<p begin="02:18:14.000" end="02:18:19.120" style="s2">Do you have enough enchanted gear? <br />I can leave you some more. Leon,  </p>
<p begin="02:18:19.120" end="02:18:23.599" style="s2">let go. I&#39;m only looking. I want Take <br />all of these. I have plenty more.</p>
<p begin="02:18:28.960" end="02:18:37.280" style="s2">That&#39;s enough. Papa older. My <br />dimensional satchel is almost full.</p>
<p begin="02:18:37.280" end="02:18:44.000" style="s2">Needle. Come home to Evergreen Village. The <br />world beyond is too dangerous. You&#39;ll be safer  </p>
<p begin="02:18:44.000" end="02:18:52.399" style="s2">with us. I&#39;m not going back. Papa older. I <br />need to make a place for myself out here.  </p>
<p begin="02:18:53.439" end="02:18:58.520" style="s2">Then someday I can protect all of you.</p>
<p begin="02:18:58.520" end="02:19:11.439" style="s2">[snorts] All grown up. Already <br />planning to protect your old man.</p>
<p begin="02:19:11.439" end="02:19:14.719" style="s2">All right. Train hard out <br />here. If anyone bullies you,  </p>
<p begin="02:19:14.720" end="02:19:20.640" style="s2">bury them in enchanted gear. <br />Don&#39;t hold back. I have plenty.</p>
<p begin="02:19:23.359" end="02:19:28.880" style="s2">That&#39;s Nah&#39;s father. He swapped the <br />beast king aside and wiped out the  </p>
<p begin="02:19:28.880" end="02:19:33.840" style="s2">entire horde with one strike. Did <br />you see that pile of infanted gear?  </p>
<p begin="02:19:33.840" end="02:19:40.960" style="s2">Any one of those could be an academy <br />treasure. And he says he has plenty.</p>
<p begin="02:19:40.960" end="02:19:55.680" style="s2">How valiant. I&#39;m only looking. I swear. Just <br />looking. Your father is a good man. Yeah.</p>
<p begin="02:19:55.680" end="02:20:02.400" style="s2">[laughter]</p>
<p begin="02:20:02.399" end="02:20:10.479" style="s2">Did they really seal Nikxar <br />back inside Ember Rift?</p>
<p begin="02:20:10.479" end="02:20:15.679" style="s2">Yes. Papa shattered his primal thunder core <br />with that strike and destroyed his power.  </p>
<p begin="02:20:16.240" end="02:20:21.519" style="s2">Nyxar is sealed in the deepest chamber <br />again. He&#39;ll never see daylight. What  </p>
<p begin="02:20:21.520" end="02:20:26.960" style="s2">about Livia? Her manacor was destroyed. <br />She was expelled from the academy and  </p>
<p begin="02:20:26.960" end="02:20:38.080" style="s2">permanently barred from readmission. <br />She got exactly what she deserved.</p>
<p begin="02:20:38.080" end="02:20:44.559" style="s2">You held a cauldron seper and <br />didn&#39;t invite your mentor.</p>
<p begin="02:20:44.560" end="02:20:45.121" style="s2">Liar.</p>
<p begin="02:20:52.399" end="02:20:59.120" style="s2">I heard what happened with the beast <br />horde. You all did well. I&#39;ve ordered  </p>
<p begin="02:20:59.120" end="02:21:04.880" style="s2">double merit points for each of you. There&#39;s <br />something you should know. Before long,  </p>
<p begin="02:21:04.880" end="02:21:10.640" style="s2">Ast will join the other six arcanemies on <br />an expedition into an ancient realm. Each  </p>
<p begin="02:21:10.640" end="02:21:16.320" style="s2">academy will choose a team of students <br />to enter. All seven arcanemies exploring  </p>
<p begin="02:21:16.319" end="02:21:21.599" style="s2">one ancient realm. There has to be <br />a fortune in there. Treasure maybe,  </p>
<p begin="02:21:21.600" end="02:21:29.360" style="s2">but there will almost certainly be an Everlife <br />Sigal. You need to find it. An Everlife Signal?  </p>
<p begin="02:21:29.359" end="02:21:41.280" style="s2">What&#39;s that? You&#39;ll learn when the time comes. <br />I have to go. I&#39;m due at the Chancellor&#39;s Tower.</p>
<p begin="02:21:41.280" end="02:21:44.000" style="s2">A realm where I can earn Aether crystals.  </p>
<p begin="02:21:44.000" end="02:21:56.240" style="s2">Count me in, pies. Wipe your mouth. We <br />haven&#39;t even seen the treasure yet. [laughter]</p>
<p begin="02:21:56.240" end="02:21:59.599" style="s2">An ancient realm sounds dangerous. <br />I think I&#39;ll stay in Guard House  </p>
<p begin="02:21:59.600" end="02:22:06.640" style="s2">Valiant. An expedition with all seven arcanemies.</p>
<p begin="02:22:06.640" end="02:22:10.480" style="s2">That actually sounds fun.</p>
</div>
</body>
</tt>
